#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""media: Seerr + Radarr + Sonarr CLI for the owner's media server (Emby is the player).

Keys go by handle through core.egress (seerr, radarr, sonarr, emby; local mode reads ~/.secrets/media.json; tracearr:
~/.secrets/tracearr-key, hub mode needs no file) and are never printed; base URLs come from the profile
(services.<svc>_url; media.json's url while the file exists).

  media search "title" [--type movie|tv] [-n 8] [--json]
  media request TMDB_ID --type movie|tv [--seasons all|1,2] [--dry-run] [--json]
  media status "title" [--type movie|tv] [--tmdb ID] [-n 1] [--json]
  media queue [--json]
  media recent [-n 15] [--json]
  (--json on these five: the typed tools' shape, packages/tools/domains/media.py in ~/opt/assistant)

Read-only extras (GET only; they never change, delete or request anything):
  media airing [--days 7] [--cinema] [--json]        episodes + movie releases, Zurich time
  media missing [-n 10] [--json]                     wanted/missing, summarized
  media cutoff [-n 10] [--json]                      below quality cutoff (upgrade candidates)
  media health [--quiet] [--json]                    arr /health + Seerr status; exit 2 on problems
  media trending [--type T] [-n 10] [--new] [--json] Seerr/TMDB trending
  media similar "title" [--type T] [--tmdb ID] [-n 10] [--new] [--json]
  media hogs [--top 20] [--type T] [--sort size|stale] [--json]   biggest titles on disk
  media unwatched [--top 15] [--type T] [--days 180] [--min-age 90] [--report [FILE]] [--no-emby] [--json]
    cleanup candidates: titles nobody played for --days (default 180) that arrived over --min-age days ago, ranked
    by size x idle time, with last play (any user), plays in 90/365 d, distinct viewers, requester and, for big
    shows, stale seasons. Play history = Tracearr (v2 public API, ids) from its first record + Emby's Playback
    Reporting DB before that (the dispatcher's read-only `emby-sql` verb: sqlite3 -readonly, immutable=1, no
    locks, no writes).
    --report writes the full markdown table (default ~/reports/media/unwatched-DATE.md); --no-emby = Tracearr only.

"Ready" pings (cron every 10 min, no tokens; GET-only on the APIs, writes only its own state + tg):
  media ready-watch [--dry-run] [--status]
    Texts the owner once per title when one of HIS Seerr requests (user MEDIA_READY_USER, default: profile services.seerr_user)
    becomes available: "🎬 Title (year) is ready on Emby" (Seerr media status 5 = on Emby), and new episodes
    of shows he requested, batched per show per run: "📺 Show S02E03–E05 ready" (Sonarr import history;
    upgrades of existing files are skipped). More than 4 at once -> one combined message. The first run (and
    the first successful run of each part) only records a baseline. Quiet hours (MEDIA_READY_QUIET, default
    0-8 Zurich, "off" disables) hold pings until the next run after 08:00; undelivered pings are retried
    (dropped after 3 days). 18 failed runs in a row (~3 h) -> one note in ~/inbox. --dry-run prints what it
    would send and saves nothing. State: ~/.local/state/media-ready/state.json.

Play on the TV (off unless ~/.config/media/play.json {"enabled": true, "tv", "wake", "device", ...}):
  media play ITEM_ID [--target DEVICE] [--dry-run [--probe]] [--from-start] [--no-wake] [--json]
    Wakes the TV (its own turn_on, else the "wake" entity over HDMI-CEC), opens the Emby app (select_source),
    finds the app's remote-controllable Emby session and sends PlayNow (from the resume point), then reads back
    NowPlayingItem. Exit 0 playing, 1 error, 2 refused/not enabled, 3 sent but not confirmed. Emby: an "emby"
    {url,key} entry. With play enabled, tonight's library picks get a "📺 Play on TV" button {"data": "mt:play:ITEM_ID"}.
    Target by bitrate: devices.json (MEDIA_PLAY_DEVICES, default ~/.config/emby/devices.json) {"<DeviceName
    substring>": {"lan_mbit": N, "prefer_over_mbit": N, "client": "...", "source": "...", "label": "..."}, all
    optional}. When the item's default media source is above the play.json device's limit (prefer_over_mbit, else
    80% of lan_mbit), another devices.json device that fits and has a remote-controllable Emby session on the LAN
    plays it instead (the TV is woken as usual and switched to that device's "source" input when one is set). No such
    device online: the TV app plays it anyway, plus a one-line stutter hint. --target DEVICE (a devices.json name or
    label, or the play.json device) skips the choice. --dry-run sends nothing to HA or any player: it reads the
    item (and, when the choice needs them, the sessions) with Emby GETs, prints the choice and the exact calls;
    --probe adds the read-only HA states.

Movie night (GET-only on Seerr, read-only Emby SQL; writes only its own state file):
  media tonight [--json] [--mood X] [--time MIN] [--args "light 90"] [--more] [--dry-run]
    Three picks with a one-line reason each: A an unwatched library movie (his Emby user), B the next unwatched
    episode of a show in progress (else a well-rated show he hasn't started), C a well-rated or trending movie that
    is not on the server or requested (Seerr discover; request it with `media request TMDB --type movie`).
    Taste = his Emby plays (genres weighted by recency, relative to how common they are in the library); his Emby
    user = the Seerr user's linked Emby account (MEDIA_TONIGHT_USER, default as ready-watch), matched to Emby's
    internal user by play overlap once and cached. --time keeps runtimes within MIN; --mood (light, dark, funny,
    action, mind, learn, ... or a genre) prefers those genres; --args parses free text ("light 90", "1h30 scifi").
    Ratings (Emby's, 0..10): a library title under 6.0 only when nothing rated better fits; the leading candidates'
    ratings are damped by TMDB's vote count (Seerr), and an unchecked one above 9.5 counts as unknown. A quality word
    ("good", "great", "best", "top", "gute" ...) sets a 7.0 floor while anything reaches it and ranks rating x taste.
    B's "📺 Play on TV" id is always the episode shown; its link is that episode, or the show's page for a new show.
    Picks aren't repeated for 14 days (next episodes: 2); --more = 3 new picks with the last run's mood and time;
    --dry-run remembers nothing. --json adds "message" (Telegram rich Markdown) and "buttons" (rows: Emby deep
    links, {"data": "mt:req:TMDB"} for C, {"data": "mt:more"}). State: ~/.local/state/media/tonight.json.

Continue watching (GET-only on Emby; writes nothing):
  media continue [--json] [-n 4]
    His Emby Continue watching, newest first: partly watched movies and episodes plus the next episode of shows in
    progress (Resume, which Emby 4.9+ merges with Next Up; /Shows/NextUp adds what it lacks, one entry per show), each
    with how far in ("45 of 110 min" or "next up") and when he last watched it (a next episode: his last play of the
    show). His Emby user is the one tonight uses (the Seerr user's linked Emby account; MEDIA_CONTINUE_EMBY_USER, a
    32-hex Emby user id, skips Seerr). --json adds "message" (Telegram rich Markdown) and "buttons" (one row each,
    {"text": "📺 <short title>", "data": "mt:play:<movie or episode id>"}, never a series id; none while play is off).
    -n at most 8. Exit 3 when Next Up failed (Resume still shown). Tonight's card gets one "▶ Continue <title>"
    button (mt:play) for the newest item watched within 14 days that isn't one of its own picks (play enabled only).
  media group [--with NAME,NAME] [--mood X] [--time MIN] [--args "Ana Ben comedy 2h"] [-n 4] [--json]
    Movie night with friends: N library movies (default 4, at most 8) that nobody in the group has played or partly
    watched, ★7+ while enough fit (ratings checked against TMDB's vote count as in tonight), mixed lead genres, each
    with runtime, rating and a one-line why. The group is him plus the named Emby users (exact name, first word or a
    unique prefix; accents ignored), default: him plus every enabled Emby user with a Playback Reporting play in the
    last 180 days. Seen = Emby's played or resumable movies per member (same TMDB id counts too) plus their Playback
    Reporting movie plays of 20+ min. --args: moods, genres and a time as in tonight; other words are names. --json adds
    "message" (Telegram rich Markdown, names only the members), "poll" (send_poll's arguments: question, options,
    anonymous false, multiple false; null under 2 picks) and "buttons" (one row per pick: ▶ Emby link + 📺 Play on TV
    mt:play:<id> while play is enabled). Read-only, remembers nothing. Exit 3 when a member's history didn't load.

  media vibe "TEXT" [-n 4] [--series] [--json]  |  media vibe --refresh [--full] [--quiet]
    4 library movies for a mood ("cozy rainy sunday"), a film ("like Arrival", "Arrival"; + words: "darker like
    Arrival") or both; "short"/"kurz" = <= 100 min, "90min"/"under 2h" = a cap. Local EmbeddingGemma index of his Emby
    movie metadata (MEDIA_VIBE_DIR, default ~/.local/state/vibe; llama-server started per run on a free loopback port,
    MEDIA_VIBE_SERVER/_MODEL, or MEDIA_VIBE_EMBED_URL = an OpenAI-style /v1/embeddings endpoint). Ranking: similarity,
    rating tilt, his played (partly watched: half) titles lower, rated 6.5+ first, genres kept apart. A query embeds
    up to 48 new titles itself; --refresh (cron, nightly) syncs the rest. Emby + Seerr GET-only; only his own
    played state. JSON: message (Markdown) + buttons (▶ link, 📺 mt:play:<id>) for the session, text (plain, links)
    for the instant /vibe; no text = a usage hint.
    Series: --series (--tv), or a series word in the text ("a dark crime series", "a show", "eine Serie", "serija"; never
    inside "like <title>"; a bare movie title stays a movie), or "like <title>" / a bare title naming a series but no
    movie -> 4 library series from a second index (series-index.json, same model; TMDB TV genres like "Sci-Fi &
    Fantasy" mapped). Unwatched and barely started shows (<= 2 episodes or 25 % watched) rank first; half-watched ones
    lower, finished ones lowest (his own Emby user data). Series picks get ▶ links only (no play button). --refresh
    updates both indexes.

  media finish [-n 5] [--days 14] [--json]
    Shows he started but didn't finish: his own Emby user only, regular episodes (no specials) played > 0, unplayed
    left, no play in more than --days days; ranked by how close he is to the end (share watched, episodes left) and
    the show rating. "Hijack · 3 of 8 left · ★7.4" + the next episode: the first unplayed one in season/episode
    order after the furthest he got to (its resume point when started), plus "skipped S01E03" for unplayed ones
    before it. Shows with only skipped ones left rank last ("watched to S03E08 · skipped S02E01–E03"). JSON: message
    (Markdown) + buttons (📺 mt:play:<episode id> while play is enabled, as in continue) for the session, text (plain,
    ▶ Emby links) for the instant /finish. GET-only. Exit 3 when some shows didn't load.

franchise [--min-owned 2] [-n 15] [--json | --poll-json]: film series (Radarr's TMDB collections) where he owns at least
    --min-owned parts (Radarr file, or available on Emby per Seerr) and a released part is missing, best first
    (shrunk TMDB rating + series popularity + share owned). Skipped: parts requested in Seerr, in Radarr (wanted,
    downloading or unmonitored = his choice), on Radarr's exclusion list or Seerr's blocklist, unreleased, and
    ignored series. Read-only. --poll-json = send_poll arguments (<= 10 options "Series: Title (year)", at most
    3 per series, multiple choice, non-anonymous) + the TMDB ids; saved for --picked.
    franchise request TMDB_ID ... | --picked 'OPTION | OPTION' [--dry-run]: Seerr requests through `request`'s path.
    franchise ignore|unignore COLLECTION_ID|NAME ...; franchise ignored [--json]. State: MEDIA_FRANCHISE_STATE
    (default ~/.local/state/franchise: ignore.json, last-poll.json).

wrapped [--year Y] [--json] [--html [OUT]] [--no-covers]: his Emby year in review (this year so far by default):
    hours, films, episodes, top genres and shows, binge record, favourite weekday and hour, most rewatched, first and
    latest play, films by decade, 4K share, a fun fact. Source: Emby's Playback Reporting rows of HIS Emby user only
    (his Seerr user's linked Emby account; filtered in the SQL) + library.db metadata, read-only; a play = one item on
    one viewing day (05:00-04:59) with >= 2 min, capped at 1.25x its runtime. Prints a <= 8-line card; --html writes an
    offline single-file story page (dark, phone-sized; covers as small embedded thumbnails via Emby's image API, GET,
    <= ~2.2 MB in all). Env MEDIA_WRAPPED_GUID (his Emby user id, skips the Seerr lookup).

doctor [TITLE | --all] [--days 180] [--type T] [--mine] [--dry-run] [--no-probe] [--grab] [-n 15] [--json]: why a Seerr
    request (his or a friend's) hasn't reached Emby yet: one verdict per request + a German and an English line he can
    forward. --all (default without TITLE): pending requests, approved ones whose title is pending/processing/partly
    there, failed ones of the last 90 days; requests older than --days and approved ones whose title Seerr reset to
    unknown/deleted (removed from the arr on purpose) are skipped and counted. Output: stuck ones in full, "waiting
    normally" (downloading, not out yet, airing) one line each, "already there or gone" counted.
    Checks: Radarr/Sonarr title (monitored, file, release dates, episodes aired vs on disk), queue (%/ETA, failed,
    stalled, import blocked), grab history, an interactive indexer search (GET /release: none / usable / all rejected
    and why, e.g. a name/year mismatch), Emby by provider id or name (already there under another id).
    Routine fixes (his standing OK; library files are never deleted or replaced): monitor the requested movie /
    seasons / episodes again; search again (MoviesSearch / EpisodeSearch, at most every 7 days per title,
    MEDIA_DOCTOR_SEARCH_DAYS); a failed or 48 h+ stalled download -> DELETE the queue item with blocklist (the arr grabs
    another); a FAILED Seerr request of the last 90 days -> POST .../retry when the arr can find the title (every 3
    days at most). Approved requests whose title left the arr are never re-added. Indexer searches: cached 7 days, at
    most 12 per run (MEDIA_DOCTOR_PROBES). --grab (TITLE, movies, owner's word only): POST /api/v3/release of the best
    release Radarr rejected only as an unknown title whose name carries the movie's title and a year within +-1, in a
    quality the profile allows. --dry-run sends no fix and saves nothing. State + action log:
    ~/.local/state/media/doctor.json + doctor.log (MEDIA_DOCTOR_STATE). --json: items, "message" (session Markdown),
    "text" (plain, the instant /doctor).
    --cron (weekly cron job): --all with the routine fixes and one summary line; writes ~/inbox/media-doctor-DATE.md
    (MEDIA_DOCTOR_INBOX) only when MEDIA_DOCTOR_NOTE_MIN (default 3) or more requests stay stuck on him (mismatch,
    rejected, import blocked, waiting for approval), else silent; exit 3 when a check failed (cron-fail notes it).
    With --dry-run it prints the note instead and fixes nothing.

  media poster ID [ID ...] [--width 400] [--json]
    Emby Primary images (GET, key in a header) of item ids for picture cards (tg-cmd /finish, /vibe, /emby), cached
    as JPEG in ~/.cache/media/posters (MEDIA_POSTER_CACHE) for 30 days (MEDIA_POSTER_MAX_AGE_DAYS); up to 12 ids,
    6 at a time, MEDIA_TIMEOUT capped at 6 s each. Prints "ID PATH" per id ("-" = no poster), --json
    {"posters": {id: path|null}, "fetched", "cached", "warnings"}; exit 3 when a poster failed to load (not a 404).

  media posters [--days 7] [--max 24] [--out PATH] [--cron] [--json]
    The "Neu auf dem Server · KW NN" collage: one dark 1080 px PNG (Pillow) of the movies and shows Emby added in the
    last N days (his Emby user's visible movie/TV libraries minus his My Media / Latest excludes), posters from Emby's
    image API with title, year and a star rating; shows grouped by series with the new episodes counted (badge);
    specials, missing episodes and extras left out; upgrades, replacements and renames (Radarr/Sonarr history: file
    deletions or renames in the window >= imports) aren't new. Over --max (MEDIA_POSTERS_MAX, 24): the best rated per section (each gets half if it can use it) plus
    "+N more". Default OUT ~/reports/media/new-on-server-DATE.png (MEDIA_REPORT_DIR). --cron also writes
    ~/inbox/media-posters-DATE.md (MEDIA_POSTERS_INBOX) with the path, counts, caption and send: yes when
    MEDIA_POSTERS_SEND_MIN (5)+ items; nothing (no image, no note) when nothing is new. GET-only; exit 3 on a warning
    (an arr's history failed: upgrades then not filtered; a poster didn't load: placeholder tile). Fonts: MEDIA_POSTERS_FONTS (default /usr/share/fonts/truetype).

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 health problems
 (health only), 3 partial result (one service failed).
Env (mostly for tests): MEDIA_SECRETS (config path), MEDIA_TIMEOUT (seconds, default 30),
MEDIA_NOW (ISO time or epoch: fake clock), MEDIA_PAGE_SIZE (arr/Seerr page size, default 500);
unwatched: MEDIA_TRACEARR_KEYFILE (default ~/.secrets/tracearr-key; or a "tracearr" {url,key} entry in the
config), MEDIA_EMBY_SQL (shell command: SQL on stdin -> sqlite3 -ascii rows; {dir} = MEDIA_EMBY_DIR, default
/mnt/user/appdata/EmbyServer/data), MEDIA_REPORT_DIR (default ~/reports/media);
ready-watch: MEDIA_READY_STATE (state dir), MEDIA_READY_USER, MEDIA_READY_TG (a test sender taking TEXT; default `tg --soft`),
MEDIA_READY_QUIET, MEDIA_READY_INBOX (default ~/inbox), MEDIA_READY_FAIL_NOTE (default 18);
play: MEDIA_PLAY_CONFIG, MEDIA_PLAY_DEVICES, MEDIA_PLAY_TV/_WAKE/_APP/_DEVICE/_CLIENT (override play.json, never "enabled"),
MEDIA_HA_BIN (default ~/bin/ha), MEDIA_PLAY_WAIT/_CONFIRM/_POLL (seconds), MEDIA_PLAY_LOCK;
tonight: MEDIA_TONIGHT_STATE (state file), MEDIA_TONIGHT_USER (Seerr user), MEDIA_TONIGHT_EMBY_UID (Emby's internal
user id, skips the mapping); continue: MEDIA_CONTINUE_EMBY_USER (Emby user id, skips the Seerr lookup).
"""
import argparse, base64, collections, fcntl, hashlib, http.client, json, math, operator, os, re, socket, subprocess, sys, time, unicodedata
import html, ipaddress, urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request
from datetime import date, datetime, timedelta, timezone
from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "lib"))
import botlib  # noqa: E402
import assistant_profile  # noqa: E402
try:    # keys by handle (core.egress)
    from core import egress as _egress  # noqa: E402
except Exception:   # a copy without ~/bin/lib: the direct path
    _egress = None

SECRETS = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("MEDIA_SECRETS") or "~/.secrets/media.json")
# The live default config (~/.secrets/media.json, core.egress importable): each media.json service's base URL
# comes from the profile (services.<svc>_url; the file's url while it exists) and its key by handle, so a
# missing live file is not fatal. A test's own config (MEDIA_SECRETS) keeps its own url/key fields.
LIVE = _egress is not None and os.path.realpath(SECRETS) == os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser("~/.secrets/media.json"))
try:
    with open(SECRETS) as f:
        CFG = json.load(f)
except Exception as e:
    if not (LIVE and isinstance(e, FileNotFoundError)):
        sys.exit(f"media: cannot read {SECRETS}: {type(e).__name__}")
    CFG = {}
# Services whose key comes from a live key file that core.egress reads too (media.json here, tracearr-key in
# tracearr_cfg): their key is egress.secret(svc) and their calls go through egress.open. A test's own config
# (MEDIA_SECRETS, MEDIA_TRACEARR_KEYFILE) keeps the direct path.
EG = set()
if LIVE:
    for _s, (_file, _f) in _egress.HANDLES.items():
        if _file == "media.json":
            EG.add(_s)
            _c = CFG.get(_s) or {}
            _u = assistant_profile.service_url(_s, _c.get("url"))
            if _u:  # "key" only says "configured": an EG key always comes from svc_key (by handle)
                CFG[_s] = dict(_c, url=_u, key=_c.get("key") or _egress.PLACEHOLDER + _s)


def _env_num(name, default):
    try:
        v = float(os.environ.get(name) or default)
        return v if v > 0 else default
    except ValueError:
        return default


TIMEOUT = _env_num("MEDIA_TIMEOUT", 30)
PAGE = int(_env_num("MEDIA_PAGE_SIZE", 500))
ZRH = assistant_profile.tz()
WD = ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"]

# Seerr (Overseerr/Jellyseerr) enums
MEDIA_STATUS = {1: "not requested", 2: "requested (pending)", 3: "requested (processing)",
                4: "partially available", 5: "available", 6: "blocklisted", 7: "deleted"}
REQ_STATUS = {1: "pending approval", 2: "approved", 3: "declined", 4: "failed", 5: "completed"}
ACTIVE = {2, 3, 4, 5}  # media/season statuses that mean "already handled, don't request again"


def die(msg, code=1):
    print(f"media: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(code)


class ApiError(Exception):
    """A Seerr/arr call failed; the message is safe to show (never contains keys)."""


def svc_key(svc):
    """svc's key: by handle when it comes from a live key file (EG; hub mode: a placeholder), else the config's."""
    if svc in EG:
        try:
            return _egress.secret(svc)
        except (KeyError, ValueError):
            raise ApiError(f"no {svc} key by handle (core.egress {svc}, {_egress.mode(svc)} mode)") from None
    return (CFG.get(svc) or {})["key"]


def svc_open(svc, req, timeout):
    """urllib.request.urlopen, through core.egress for a service in EG (same errors; hub refusals are URLErrors)."""
    if svc in EG:
        return _egress.open(req, svc, timeout=timeout)
    return urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout)


def api(svc, method, path, body=None, timeout=None):
    timeout = timeout or TIMEOUT
    c = CFG.get(svc) or {}
    if not c.get("url") or not c.get("key"):
        raise ApiError(f"no {svc} url (profile services.{svc}_url)" if svc in EG and svc != "tracearr"
                       else f"no {svc} url/key in {SECRETS}")
    url = c["url"].rstrip("/") + path
    where = f"{method} {path.split('?')[0]}"
    h = {"Accept": "application/json"}
    if svc == "tracearr":                       # Tracearr's public API wants a bearer token
        h["Authorization"] = f"Bearer {svc_key(svc)}"
    elif svc == "emby":                         # Emby API key (Dashboard > Advanced > Security)
        h["X-Emby-Token"] = svc_key(svc)
    else:
        h["X-Api-Key"] = svc_key(svc)
    data = None
    if body is not None:
        data = json.dumps(body).encode()
        h["Content-Type"] = "application/json"
    try:
        with svc_open(svc, urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers=h, method=method), timeout) as r:
            raw = r.read()
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        detail = e.read().decode(errors="replace")[:400]
        raise ApiError(f"{svc} HTTP {e.code} on {where}: {detail}")
    except urllib.error.URLError as e:
        if isinstance(e.reason, (TimeoutError, socket.timeout)):
            raise ApiError(f"{svc} timed out after {timeout:g}s on {where}")
        raise ApiError(f"cannot reach {svc}: {e.reason}")
    except (TimeoutError, socket.timeout):
        raise ApiError(f"{svc} timed out after {timeout:g}s on {where}")
    except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as e:
        raise ApiError(f"cannot reach {svc}: {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
    try:
        return json.loads(raw) if raw else None
    except ValueError:
        raise ApiError(f"{svc} sent non-JSON on {where} (wrong URL, or a login page?)")


def get(svc, path, timeout=None):
    return api(svc, "GET", path, timeout=timeout)


def q(s):
    return urllib.parse.quote(str(s), safe="")


def now_utc():
    v = os.environ.get("MEDIA_NOW")
    if v:
        try:
            return datetime.fromtimestamp(float(v), timezone.utc)
        except ValueError:
            d = datetime.fromisoformat(v.replace("Z", "+00:00"))
            return (d if d.tzinfo else d.replace(tzinfo=ZRH)).astimezone(timezone.utc)
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc)


def zdt(s):
    """ISO timestamp from an arr/Seerr API -> aware datetime, or None."""
    if not s:
        return None
    try:
        d = datetime.fromisoformat(str(s).replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return d if d.tzinfo else d.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)


def iso_z(d):
    return d.astimezone(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def dlabel(d):
    return f"{WD[d.weekday()]} {d:%d.%m}"


def ldate(d, fmt="%d.%m.%Y"):
    """Zurich-local date string of an aware datetime ('?' if None)."""
    return d.astimezone(ZRH).strftime(fmt) if d else "?"


def fmt_bytes(n):
    n = float(n or 0)
    for unit in ("B", "kB", "MB", "GB", "TB", "PB"):
        if n < 1000 or unit == "PB":
            return f"{n:.0f} {unit}" if unit in ("B", "kB") or n >= 100 else f"{n:.1f} {unit}"
        n /= 1000.0


def emit_json(obj):
    print(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1,
                     default=lambda o: o.isoformat() if hasattr(o, "isoformat") else str(o)))


def soft(fn, warns, label):
    """Run one service's part; on failure note it and carry on with the rest."""
    try:
        return fn()
    except ApiError as e:
        warns.append(f"{label}: {e}")
        return None


def finish(warns, as_json=False):
    """Print skipped-service notes; exit 3 if a part failed."""
    if warns:
        if not as_json:
            for w in warns:
                print(f"!! skipped {w}")
        sys.exit(3)


def more(lst, n, indent="  "):
    if len(lst) > n:
        print(f"{indent}… +{len(lst) - n} more")


def section(head, rows, n, line):
    """`head`, then the first n rows as '  line(row)' and '… +N more'; nothing at all for no rows."""
    if rows:
        print(head)
        for r in rows[:n]:
            print("  " + line(r))
        more(rows, n)


def year(x):
    d = x.get("releaseDate") or x.get("firstAirDate") or ""
    return d[:4] or "????"


def title_of(x):
    return x.get("title") or x.get("name") or "?"


def eta(rec):
    if rec.get("size") and not rec.get("sizeleft"):
        return "done, importing"
    t = rec.get("estimatedCompletionTime")
    if not t:
        return rec.get("timeleft") or "?"
    try:
        dt = datetime.fromisoformat(t.replace("Z", "+00:00"))
        mins = int((dt - now_utc()).total_seconds() // 60)
        if mins <= 0:
            return "any moment"
        local = dt.astimezone(ZRH).strftime("%H:%M" if mins < 1200 else "%a %H:%M")
        return f"{mins // 60}h{mins % 60:02d}m (~{local})" if mins >= 60 else f"{mins}m (~{local})"
    except ValueError:
        return rec.get("timeleft") or "?"


def eta_txt(rec):
    e = eta(rec)
    return e if e == "done, importing" else f"ETA {e}"


def pct(rec):
    size, left = rec.get("size") or 0, rec.get("sizeleft") or 0
    return f"{100 * (size - left) / size:.0f}%" if size else "?%"


def issue(rec):
    """Short problem note for a queue record (import blocked, warnings, ...)."""
    state = rec.get("trackedDownloadState") or ""
    st = rec.get("trackedDownloadStatus") or ""
    msgs = [m for sm in rec.get("statusMessages") or [] for m in sm.get("messages", [])]
    if rec.get("errorMessage"):
        msgs.insert(0, rec["errorMessage"])
    bad = st in ("warning", "error") or state in ("importBlocked", "importFailed", "failedPending", "failed")
    if not bad:
        return ""
    return f"  !! {state or st}: {msgs[0][:160] if msgs else 'see the arr UI'}"


# ---------- Seerr helpers ----------

def seerr_search(query, mtype=None, n=8):
    d = api("seerr", "GET", f"/api/v1/search?query={q(query)}&page=1&language=en")
    res = [x for x in d.get("results", []) if x.get("mediaType") in ("movie", "tv")]
    if mtype:
        res = [x for x in res if x["mediaType"] == mtype]
    return res[:n]


def details(tmdb, mtype):
    return api("seerr", "GET", f"/api/v1/{mtype}/{int(tmdb)}?language=en")


def open_requests(mi):
    return [r for r in (mi or {}).get("requests") or [] if r.get("status") in (1, 2) and not r.get("is4k")]


def status_label(mi):
    if not mi:
        return MEDIA_STATUS[1]
    s = MEDIA_STATUS.get(mi.get("status"), f"status {mi.get('status')}")
    pend = [r for r in open_requests(mi) if r.get("status") == 1]
    if pend and mi.get("status") in (1, 7):
        s = "requested (pending approval)"
    return s


def season_state(det):
    """{season: label} for a TV show, from Seerr's season statuses and open requests."""
    mi = det.get("mediaInfo") or {}
    st = {s["seasonNumber"]: s["status"] for s in mi.get("seasons") or []}
    reqd = {s["seasonNumber"] for r in open_requests(mi) for s in r.get("seasons") or []}
    out = {}
    for s in det.get("seasons") or []:
        n = s["seasonNumber"]
        if n == 0:
            continue
        code = st.get(n, 1)
        if code in ACTIVE:
            out[n] = MEDIA_STATUS[code]
        elif n in reqd:
            out[n] = "requested"
        else:
            out[n] = None  # free to request
    return out


# ---------- commands ----------

def hit_json(x):
    return {"title": title_of(x), "year": year(x), "type": x["mediaType"], "tmdb": x["id"],
            "status": status_label(x.get("mediaInfo"))}


def queue_json(rec, svc, group=None):
    """One download (a Radarr record, or a Sonarr group of records) as a dict: what the text line shows."""
    st = rec.get("trackedDownloadState") or rec.get("trackedDownloadStatus") or ""
    d = {"progress": pct(rec), "status": rec.get("status"), "eta": eta(rec), "issue": issue(rec).strip()[3:] or None,
         "state": st or None}
    if svc == "radarr":
        m = rec.get("movie") or {}
        return dict({"title": m.get("title", rec.get("title")), "year": m.get("year"), "tmdb": m.get("tmdbId")}, **d)
    eps = sorted((r.get("episode") or {}).get("episodeNumber", 0) for r in group or [rec])
    sn = rec.get("seasonNumber", (rec.get("episode") or {}).get("seasonNumber", 0))
    return dict({"series": (rec.get("series") or {}).get("title", "?"), "tmdb": (rec.get("series") or {}).get("tmdbId"),
                 "season": sn, "episodes": eps,
                 "episode_title": (rec.get("episode") or {}).get("title") if len(eps) == 1 else None}, **d)


def cmd_search(a):
    res = seerr_search(a.query, a.type, a.n)
    if getattr(a, "json", False):
        print(json.dumps([hit_json(x) for x in res], ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))
        return
    if not res:
        print("no results")
        return
    for x in res:
        print(f"{title_of(x)} ({year(x)})  [{x['mediaType']}]  tmdb:{x['id']}  -- {status_label(x.get('mediaInfo'))}")


def cmd_request(a):
    det = details(a.tmdb_id, a.type)
    name = f"{title_of(det)} ({year(det)})"
    mi = det.get("mediaInfo") or {}
    if mi.get("status") == 6:
        die(f"{name} is on Seerr's blocklist; not requesting.")
    body = {"mediaType": a.type, "mediaId": int(a.tmdb_id), "is4k": False}

    js = getattr(a, "json", False)
    res = {"title": name, "type": a.type, "tmdb": int(a.tmdb_id)}
    if a.type == "movie":
        if mi.get("status") in ACTIVE or open_requests(mi):
            if js:
                print(json.dumps(dict(res, result="not_requested", reason=f"already {status_label(mi)}"),
                                 ensure_ascii=False))
                return
            print(f"Not requested: {name} is already {status_label(mi)}.")
            return
    else:
        ss = season_state(det)
        if not ss:
            die(f"{name}: TMDB lists no seasons yet; nothing to request.")
        if a.seasons in (None, "all"):
            wanted = sorted(ss)
        else:
            try:
                wanted = sorted({int(s) for s in a.seasons.split(",") if s.strip()})
            except ValueError:
                die("--seasons must be 'all' or a list like 1,2")
            unknown = [s for s in wanted if s not in ss]
            if unknown:
                die(f"{name} has no season(s) {unknown}; it has {sorted(ss)}.")
        taken = {s: ss[s] for s in wanted if ss[s]}
        todo = [s for s in wanted if not ss[s]]
        if not todo:
            why = ", ".join(f"S{s}: {v}" for s, v in taken.items())
            if js:
                print(json.dumps(dict(res, result="not_requested", reason=f"every wanted season is already handled: {why}"),
                                 ensure_ascii=False))
                return
            print(f"Not requested: {name} -- every wanted season is already handled: " + why)
            return
        res["skipped"] = {str(s): v for s, v in taken.items()}
        if taken:
            print("skipping " + ", ".join(f"S{s} ({v})" for s, v in taken.items()), file=sys.stderr)
        body["seasons"] = todo

    if a.dry_run:
        if js:
            print(json.dumps(dict(res, result="dry_run", seasons=body.get("seasons")), ensure_ascii=False))
            return
        print(f"DRY RUN, would POST /api/v1/request {json.dumps(body)}  for {name}")
        return
    r = api("seerr", "POST", "/api/v1/request", body)
    rs = REQ_STATUS.get((r or {}).get("status"), "?")
    arr = "Radarr" if a.type == "movie" else "Sonarr"
    seasons = f" seasons {','.join(map(str, body['seasons']))}" if a.type == "tv" else ""
    tail = f", {arr} will grab it" if rs == "approved" else ""
    if js:
        print(json.dumps(dict(res, result="requested", request_id=(r or {}).get("id"), request_status=rs,
                              seasons=body.get("seasons")), ensure_ascii=False))
        return
    print(f"Requested {name}{seasons} (request #{(r or {}).get('id')}, {rs}){tail}")


def arr_queue(svc):
    if svc == "radarr":
        return api("radarr", "GET", "/api/v3/queue?page=1&pageSize=200&includeMovie=true")["records"]
    return api("sonarr", "GET", "/api/v3/queue?page=1&pageSize=200&includeSeries=true&includeEpisode=true")["records"]


def fmt_sonarr_group(recs):
    """One line per download (season packs = many records with one downloadId)."""
    r0 = recs[0]
    eps = sorted((r.get("episode") or {}).get("episodeNumber", 0) for r in recs)
    s = r0.get("seasonNumber", (r0.get("episode") or {}).get("seasonNumber", 0))
    epstr = f"S{s:02d}E{eps[0]:02d}" + (f"-E{eps[-1]:02d} ({len(eps)} eps)" if len(eps) > 1 else "")
    if len(eps) == 1 and (r0.get("episode") or {}).get("title"):
        epstr += f" \"{r0['episode']['title']}\""
    return (f"{(r0.get('series') or {}).get('title', '?')} {epstr} -- {pct(r0)}, {r0.get('status')}, "
            f"{eta_txt(r0)}{issue(r0)}")


def group_sonarr(recs):
    groups = {}
    for r in recs:
        groups.setdefault(r.get("downloadId") or r.get("id"), []).append(r)
    return list(groups.values())


def fmt_radarr(r):
    m = r.get("movie") or {}
    return f"{m.get('title', r.get('title'))} ({m.get('year', '?')}) -- {pct(r)}, {r.get('status')}, {eta_txt(r)}{issue(r)}"


def cmd_queue(a):
    rq, sq = arr_queue("radarr"), group_sonarr(arr_queue("sonarr"))
    if getattr(a, "json", False):
        print(json.dumps({"movies": [queue_json(r, "radarr") for r in rq],
                          "tv": [queue_json(g[0], "sonarr", g) for g in sq]}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))
        return
    if not rq and not sq:
        print("nothing downloading")
        return
    if rq:
        print(f"Movies ({len(rq)}):")
        for r in rq:
            print("  " + fmt_radarr(r))
    if sq:
        print(f"TV ({len(sq)}):")
        for g in sq:
            print("  " + fmt_sonarr_group(g))


def cmd_status(a):
    if a.tmdb:
        if not a.type:
            die("--tmdb needs --type movie|tv")
        hits = [{"id": a.tmdb, "mediaType": a.type}]
    else:
        if not a.title:
            die("give a title or --tmdb ID --type T")
        hits = seerr_search(a.title, a.type, 10)
        if not hits:
            print("[]" if getattr(a, "json", False) else "no results")
            return
        exact = [h for h in hits if title_of(h).lower() == a.title.lower()]
        hits = (exact + [h for h in hits if h not in exact])[: a.n]
    rq = sq = None
    js = getattr(a, "json", False)
    rows = []
    for h in hits:
        mtype = h["mediaType"]
        det = details(h["id"], mtype)
        mi = det.get("mediaInfo") or {}
        if js:
            row = {"title": title_of(det), "year": year(det), "type": mtype, "tmdb": det["id"],
                   "status": status_label(mi), "requests": [], "downloading": []}
            for r in open_requests(mi):
                row["requests"].append({"id": r["id"], "status": REQ_STATUS.get(r["status"]),
                                        "seasons": [s["seasonNumber"] for s in r.get("seasons") or []],
                                        "by": (r.get("requestedBy") or {}).get("displayName") or "?",
                                        "created": r.get("createdAt", "")[:10]})
            if mtype == "tv":
                row["seasons"] = {str(s): v or "not requested" for s, v in season_state(det).items()}
            if mi.get("mediaUrl") and mi.get("status") in (4, 5):
                row["emby_url"] = mi["mediaUrl"]
            if mtype == "movie":
                rq = arr_queue("radarr") if rq is None else rq
                row["downloading"] = [queue_json(r, "radarr") for r in rq
                                      if (r.get("movie") or {}).get("tmdbId") == det["id"]]
            else:
                sq = arr_queue("sonarr") if sq is None else sq
                row["downloading"] = [queue_json(g[0], "sonarr", g) for g in
                                      group_sonarr([r for r in sq if (r.get("series") or {}).get("tmdbId") == det["id"]])]
            if not row["downloading"] and mi.get("status") == 3:
                row["note"] = "not in the download queue right now (searching, or waiting for a release)"
            rows.append(row)
            continue
        print(f"{title_of(det)} ({year(det)})  [{mtype}]  tmdb:{det['id']}  -- {status_label(mi)}")
        for r in open_requests(mi):
            who = (r.get("requestedBy") or {}).get("displayName") or "?"
            seas = ",".join(str(s["seasonNumber"]) for s in r.get("seasons") or [])
            print(f"  request #{r['id']}: {REQ_STATUS.get(r['status'])}{' S' + seas if seas else ''} by {who}, {r.get('createdAt', '')[:10]}")
        if mtype == "tv":
            ss = season_state(det)
            if ss:
                print("  seasons: " + ", ".join(f"S{s}: {v or 'not requested'}" for s, v in ss.items()))
        if mi.get("mediaUrl") and mi.get("status") in (4, 5):
            print(f"  Emby: {mi['mediaUrl']}")
        # live download progress from the arr queues
        if mtype == "movie":
            rq = arr_queue("radarr") if rq is None else rq
            mine = [r for r in rq if (r.get("movie") or {}).get("tmdbId") == det["id"]]
            for r in mine:
                print("  downloading: " + fmt_radarr(r))
        else:
            sq = arr_queue("sonarr") if sq is None else sq
            mine = [r for r in sq if (r.get("series") or {}).get("tmdbId") == det["id"]]
            for g in group_sonarr(mine):
                print("  downloading: " + fmt_sonarr_group(g))
        if not mine and mi.get("status") == 3:
            print("  not in the download queue right now (searching, or waiting for a release)")
    if js:
        print(json.dumps(rows, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))


def cmd_recent(a):
    n = a.n
    rh = api("radarr", "GET", f"/api/v3/history?page=1&pageSize={n}&sortKey=date&sortDirection=descending"
                              "&eventType=3&includeMovie=true")["records"]
    sh = api("sonarr", "GET", f"/api/v3/history?page=1&pageSize={n * 4}&sortKey=date&sortDirection=descending"
                              "&eventType=3&includeSeries=true&includeEpisode=true")["records"]
    items, js_items = [], []
    for r in rh:
        m = r.get("movie") or {}
        items.append((r["date"], f"movie  {m.get('title', '?')} ({m.get('year', '?')})"))
        js_items.append((r["date"], {"type": "movie", "title": m.get("title", "?"), "year": m.get("year")}))
    groups = {}
    for r in sh:  # collapse episodes of one season imported on the same day
        ep = r.get("episode") or {}
        k = ((r.get("series") or {}).get("title", "?"), ep.get("seasonNumber", 0), r["date"][:10])
        g = groups.setdefault(k, {"date": r["date"], "eps": []})
        g["eps"].append(ep.get("episodeNumber", 0))
        g["date"] = max(g["date"], r["date"])
    for (title, s, _), g in groups.items():
        eps = sorted(set(g["eps"]))
        es = ",".join(f"E{e:02d}" for e in eps) if len(eps) <= 4 else f"E{eps[0]:02d}-E{eps[-1]:02d} ({len(eps)} eps)"
        items.append((g["date"], f"tv     {title} S{s:02d} {es}"))
        js_items.append((g["date"], {"type": "tv", "title": title, "season": s, "episodes": eps}))
    if getattr(a, "json", False):
        js_items.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)
        out = [dict(d, at=datetime.fromisoformat(t.replace("Z", "+00:00")).astimezone(ZRH).isoformat(timespec="minutes"))
               for t, d in js_items[:n]]
        print(json.dumps(out, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))
        return
    items.sort(reverse=True)
    for d, line in items[:n]:
        local = datetime.fromisoformat(d.replace("Z", "+00:00")).astimezone(ZRH).strftime("%a %d.%m %H:%M")
        print(f"{local}  {line}")


# ---------- read-only extras (GET only) ----------

def arr_all(svc, path, cap=20000):
    """Every record of a paged arr endpoint (wanted/missing, wanted/cutoff) -> (records, totalRecords)."""
    out, page, sep = [], 1, "&" if "?" in path else "?"
    while True:
        d = get(svc, f"{path}{sep}page={page}&pageSize={PAGE}") or {}
        recs = d.get("records") or []
        out += recs
        total = d.get("totalRecords") or len(out)
        if not recs or len(out) >= total or len(out) >= cap:
            return out, total
        page += 1


def quality_name(items, qid):
    """Name of quality or quality group `qid` inside a profile's items tree."""
    for it in items or []:
        if (it.get("quality") or {}).get("id") == qid:
            return it["quality"].get("name") or "?"
        if it.get("id") == qid and it.get("name"):
            return it["name"]
        sub = quality_name(it.get("items"), qid)
        if sub:
            return sub
    return None


def profiles(svc):
    """{profile id: (name, cutoff quality name)}"""
    return {p.get("id"): (p.get("name") or "?", quality_name(p.get("items"), p.get("cutoff")) or "?")
            for p in get(svc, "/api/v3/qualityprofile") or []}


def group_episodes(recs, titles=None):
    """Wanted episode records -> per-show summary, most episodes first."""
    shows = {}
    for r in recs:
        sid = r.get("seriesId")
        title = (r.get("series") or {}).get("title") or (titles or {}).get(sid) or f"series #{sid}"
        s = shows.setdefault(sid, {"series": title, "series_id": sid, "episodes": 0, "seasons": set(), "last_aired": None})
        s["episodes"] += 1
        s["seasons"].add(r.get("seasonNumber", 0))
        t = zdt(r.get("airDateUtc"))
        if t and (not s["last_aired"] or t > s["last_aired"]):
            s["last_aired"] = t
    out = sorted(shows.values(), key=lambda s: (-s["episodes"], -(s["last_aired"] or datetime.min.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)).timestamp()))
    for s in out:
        s["seasons"] = sorted(s["seasons"])
    return out


def seasons_txt(ss):
    return ",".join(f"S{s}" for s in ss) if len(ss) <= 4 else f"{len(ss)} seasons"


def plural(n, word):
    return f"{n} {word}{'' if n == 1 else 's'}"


def cmd_airing(a):
    if not 1 <= a.days <= 60:
        die("--days must be between 1 and 60")
    now = now_utc()
    day0 = now.astimezone(ZRH).replace(hour=0, minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)
    endl = day0 + timedelta(days=a.days)          # wall-clock days, DST-safe with zoneinfo
    s_utc, e_utc = day0.astimezone(timezone.utc), endl.astimezone(timezone.utc)
    rng = f"start={q(iso_z(s_utc))}&end={q(iso_z(e_utc))}&unmonitored=false"
    warns = []
    eps = soft(lambda: get("sonarr", f"/api/v3/calendar?{rng}&includeSeries=true"), warns, "Sonarr")
    mov = soft(lambda: get("radarr", f"/api/v3/calendar?{rng}"), warns, "Radarr")
    if eps is None and mov is None:
        die("; ".join(warns))

    groups, ep_items = {}, []
    for e in eps or []:
        t = zdt(e.get("airDateUtc"))
        if not t or not s_utc <= t < e_utc:
            continue
        lt, ser = t.astimezone(ZRH), e.get("series") or {}
        title = ser.get("title") or f"series #{e.get('seriesId')}"
        ep_items.append({"series": title, "season": e.get("seasonNumber", 0), "episode": e.get("episodeNumber", 0),
                         "title": e.get("title"), "air_utc": iso_z(t), "air_local": lt.isoformat(),
                         "has_file": bool(e.get("hasFile"))})
        k = (lt.date(), e.get("seriesId") or title, e.get("seasonNumber", 0))
        g = groups.setdefault(k, {"date": lt.date(), "time": lt, "series": title, "season": k[2], "eps": []})
        g["time"] = min(g["time"], lt)
        g["eps"].append(e)

    kinds = [("digital", "digitalRelease"), ("physical", "physicalRelease")]
    if a.cinema:
        kinds.append(("cinema", "inCinemas"))
    rels = []
    for m in mov or []:
        for kind, field in kinds:
            try:
                d = date.fromisoformat((m.get(field) or "")[:10])
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if day0.date() <= d < endl.date():
                rels.append({"date": d, "kind": kind, "title": m.get("title") or "?", "year": m.get("year"),
                             "tmdb": m.get("tmdbId"), "has_file": bool(m.get("hasFile"))})
    rels.sort(key=lambda r: (r["date"], r["title"]))

    if a.json:
        emit_json({"start": day0.isoformat(), "end": endl.isoformat(), "episodes": ep_items,
                   "movies": [dict(r, date=r["date"].isoformat()) for r in rels], "warnings": warns})
        return finish(warns, True)

    last = (endl - timedelta(days=1)).date()
    span = f"{dlabel(day0.date())} – {dlabel(last)}" if a.days > 1 else dlabel(day0.date())
    if not ep_items and not rels:
        print(f"Nothing airing {span}.")
        return finish(warns)
    print(f"Airing {span} (Zurich time, ✓ = on disk): {plural(len(ep_items), 'episode')}, "
          f"{plural(len(rels), 'movie release')}")
    for d in sorted({g["date"] for g in groups.values()} | {r["date"] for r in rels}):
        print(dlabel(d) + (" (today)" if d == day0.date() else ""))
        for g in sorted((g for g in groups.values() if g["date"] == d), key=lambda g: (g["time"], g["series"])):
            es = sorted(g["eps"], key=lambda e: e.get("episodeNumber", 0))
            n0, n1 = es[0].get("episodeNumber", 0), es[-1].get("episodeNumber", 0)
            code = f"S{g['season']:02d}E{n0:02d}" + (f"-E{n1:02d} ({len(es)} eps)" if len(es) > 1 else "")
            et = (es[0].get("title") or "").strip()
            if len(es) == 1 and et and et.upper() not in ("TBA", "TBD"):
                code += f' "{et}"'
            have = " ✓" if all(e.get("hasFile") for e in es) else ""
            print(f"  {g['time']:%H:%M} {g['series']} {code}{have}")
        for r in (r for r in rels if r["date"] == d):
            print(f"  🎬 {r['title']} ({r['year'] or '?'}) {r['kind']}{' ✓' if r['has_file'] else ''}")
    finish(warns)


def next_release(m, now):
    """(kind, date) of a missing movie's next expected release: digital/physical first, else cinema."""
    soon = now - timedelta(days=1)
    home = [(t, k) for k, f in (("digital", "digitalRelease"), ("physical", "physicalRelease"))
            for t in [zdt(m.get(f))] if t and t >= soon]
    if home:
        t, k = min(home)
        return k, t
    cin = zdt(m.get("inCinemas"))
    if cin:
        return ("cinema", cin) if cin >= soon else ("in cinemas, no digital date", None)
    return None, None


def cmd_missing(a):
    now, warns = now_utc(), []
    eps = soft(lambda: arr_all("sonarr", "/api/v3/wanted/missing?monitored=true&includeSeries=true"), warns, "Sonarr")
    mov = soft(lambda: arr_all("radarr", "/api/v3/wanted/missing?monitored=true"), warns, "Radarr")
    if eps is None and mov is None:
        die("; ".join(warns))
    ep_recs, mv_recs = (eps or ([], 0))[0], (mov or ([], 0))[0]
    shows = group_episodes(ep_recs)
    released, upcoming = [], []
    for m in mv_recs:
        item = {"title": m.get("title") or "?", "year": m.get("year"), "tmdb": m.get("tmdbId"),
                "status": m.get("status"), "added": zdt(m.get("added"))}
        if m.get("status") == "released":
            released.append(item)
        else:
            item["next"], item["next_date"] = next_release(m, now)
            upcoming.append(item)
    epoch = datetime.min.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)
    released.sort(key=lambda m: m["added"] or epoch)
    upcoming.sort(key=lambda m: (m["next_date"] is None, m["next_date"] or epoch, m["title"]))

    if a.json:
        emit_json({"episodes_total": len(ep_recs), "shows": shows, "movies_released": released,
                   "movies_not_out": upcoming, "warnings": warns})
        return finish(warns, True)
    if not ep_recs and not mv_recs:
        print("Nothing missing: every monitored, aired episode and movie is on disk.")
        return finish(warns)
    print(f"Missing (monitored, no file): {plural(len(ep_recs), 'episode')} in {plural(len(shows), 'show')}, "
          f"{len(released)} released {'movie' if len(released) == 1 else 'movies'}; {len(upcoming)} more not out yet")
    section("TV:", shows, a.n, lambda s: f"{s['series']}: {plural(s['episodes'], 'ep')} "
                                         f"({seasons_txt(s['seasons'])}), last aired {ldate(s['last_aired'])}")
    section("Movies released but not downloaded (longest wanted first):", released, a.n,
            lambda m: f"{m['title']} ({m['year'] or '?'}), wanted since {ldate(m['added'], '%m.%Y')}")
    section("Not out yet (next release):", upcoming, a.n, lambda m: f"{m['title']} ({m['year'] or '?'}): " + (
        (f"{m['next']} {ldate(m['next_date'])}" if m["next_date"] else m["next"]) or "no date yet"))
    finish(warns)


def cmd_cutoff(a):
    warns = []

    def tv():
        recs, _ = arr_all("sonarr", "/api/v3/wanted/cutoff?monitored=true")
        if not recs:
            return []
        series = {s.get("id"): s for s in get("sonarr", "/api/v3/series") or []}
        profs = profiles("sonarr")
        shows = group_episodes(recs, {k: v.get("title") for k, v in series.items()})
        for s in shows:
            prof, cut = profs.get((series.get(s["series_id"]) or {}).get("qualityProfileId"), ("?", "?"))
            s.update(profile=prof, cutoff=cut)
        return shows

    def movies():
        recs, _ = arr_all("radarr", "/api/v3/wanted/cutoff?monitored=true")
        if not recs:
            return []
        profs = profiles("radarr")
        out = []
        for m in recs:
            st = m.get("statistics") or {}
            cur = [x.get("name") for x in st.get("movieFileQualities") or [] if x.get("name")]
            if not cur and (m.get("movieFile") or {}).get("quality"):
                cur = [((m["movieFile"]["quality"].get("quality")) or {}).get("name") or "?"]
            prof, cut = profs.get(m.get("qualityProfileId"), ("?", "?"))
            out.append({"title": m.get("title") or "?", "year": m.get("year"), "tmdb": m.get("tmdbId"),
                        "quality": "/".join(cur) or "?", "profile": prof, "cutoff": cut,
                        "size": m.get("sizeOnDisk") or st.get("sizeOnDisk") or 0})
        return sorted(out, key=lambda m: m["title"].lower())

    shows = soft(tv, warns, "Sonarr")
    mv = soft(movies, warns, "Radarr")
    if shows is None and mv is None:
        die("; ".join(warns))
    shows, mv = shows or [], mv or []
    n_eps = sum(s["episodes"] for s in shows)
    if a.json:
        emit_json({"episodes_total": n_eps, "shows": shows, "movies": mv, "warnings": warns})
        return finish(warns, True)
    if not shows and not mv:
        print("Nothing below its quality cutoff.")
        return finish(warns)
    print(f"Below quality cutoff (upgrade candidates; upgrades usually need more space): "
          f"{plural(n_eps, 'episode')} in {plural(len(shows), 'show')}, {plural(len(mv), 'movie')}")
    section("TV:", shows, a.n, lambda s: f"{s['series']}: {plural(s['episodes'], 'ep')} below {s['cutoff']} "
                                         f"({s['profile']})")
    section("Movies:", mv, a.n, lambda m: f"{m['title']} ({m['year'] or '?'}): has {m['quality']}, cutoff {m['cutoff']}")
    finish(warns)


def cmd_health(a):
    problems, notes, checked = [], [], []
    for svc, name in (("sonarr", "Sonarr"), ("radarr", "Radarr")):
        try:
            items = get(svc, "/api/v3/health", timeout=min(TIMEOUT, 20)) or []
        except ApiError as e:
            problems.append({"service": name, "type": "error", "message": f"unreachable ({e})"})
            continue
        checked.append(name)
        for h in items:
            t = (h.get("type") or "warning").lower()
            wiki = h.get("wikiUrl")
            wiki = wiki.get("fullUri") if isinstance(wiki, dict) else wiki
            entry = {"service": name, "type": t, "source": h.get("source"),
                     "message": (h.get("message") or "?").strip(), "wiki": wiki}
            (notes if t in ("ok", "notice") else problems).append(entry)
    try:
        st = get("seerr", "/api/v1/status", timeout=min(TIMEOUT, 20)) or {}
        checked.append("Seerr")
        if st.get("restartRequired"):
            problems.append({"service": "Seerr", "type": "warning", "message": "restart required (settings changed)"})
        if st.get("updateAvailable"):
            behind = st.get("commitsBehind")
            notes.append({"service": "Seerr", "type": "notice",
                          "message": "update available" + (f" ({behind} commits behind)" if behind else "")})
        se = (get("seerr", "/api/v1/request?take=1&skip=0&filter=all", timeout=min(TIMEOUT, 20)) or {}).get("serviceErrors") or {}
        for svc, errs in se.items():
            if errs:
                names = ", ".join((x.get("name") if isinstance(x, dict) else str(x)) or "?" for x in errs)
                problems.append({"service": "Seerr", "type": "error", "message": f"cannot reach {svc}: {names}"})
    except ApiError as e:
        problems.append({"service": "Seerr", "type": "error", "message": f"unreachable ({e})"})

    if a.json:
        emit_json({"ok": not problems, "problems": problems, "notes": notes, "checked": checked})
    elif not problems:
        if not a.quiet:
            tail = "; ".join(f"{n['service']}: {n['message']}" for n in notes)
            print("all fine: " + ", ".join(checked) + (f" · notes: {tail}" if tail else ""))
    else:
        print(f"media health: {plural(len(problems), 'problem')}")
        for p in problems:
            print(f"  {p['service']} {p['type']}: {p['message'][:300]}")
        for n in notes:
            print(f"  ({n['service']} note: {n['message'][:200]})")
    sys.exit(2 if problems else 0)


def is_new(x):
    """Neither on the server nor requested (Seerr's view)."""
    mi = x.get("mediaInfo")
    return not mi or (mi.get("status") not in ACTIVE and mi.get("status") != 6 and not open_requests(mi))


def disc_item(x, mtype=None):
    return {"title": title_of(x), "year": year(x), "type": x.get("mediaType") or mtype, "tmdb": x.get("id"),
            "rating": round(x["voteAverage"], 1) if x.get("voteAverage") else None,
            "status": status_label(x.get("mediaInfo"))}


def disc_line(i, it):
    star = f" ★{it['rating']:.1f}" if it["rating"] else ""
    return f"{i:2d}. {it['title']} ({it['year']}) [{it['type']}]{star} tmdb:{it['tmdb']} -- {it['status']}"


def cmd_trending(a):
    items, page = [], 1
    while len(items) < a.n and page <= 5:
        d = get("seerr", f"/api/v1/discover/trending?page={page}&language=en") or {}
        for x in d.get("results") or []:
            if x.get("mediaType") in ("movie", "tv") and (not a.type or x["mediaType"] == a.type) and (not a.new or is_new(x)):
                items.append(disc_item(x))
        if page >= (d.get("totalPages") or 1):
            break
        page += 1
    items = items[:a.n]
    if a.json:
        return emit_json(items)
    if not items:
        print("nothing trending" + (" that isn't already on the server or requested" if a.new else ""))
        return
    what = {"movie": "movies", "tv": "shows"}.get(a.type, "titles")
    print(f"Trending {what} this week (TMDB via Seerr){', not on the server yet' if a.new else ''}:")
    for i, it in enumerate(items, 1):
        print(disc_line(i, it))


def cmd_similar(a):
    if a.tmdb:
        if not a.type:
            die("--tmdb needs --type movie|tv")
        base = details(a.tmdb, a.type)
        mtype = a.type
    else:
        if not a.title:
            die("give a title, or --tmdb ID --type movie|tv")
        hits = seerr_search(a.title, a.type, 10)
        if not hits:
            print(f"no match for \"{a.title}\"")
            return
        exact = [h for h in hits if title_of(h).lower() == a.title.lower()]
        base = (exact or hits)[0]
        mtype = base["mediaType"]
    tid = int(base["id"])
    res = []
    for kind in ("recommendations", "similar"):    # TMDB recommendations first, "similar" as fallback
        d = get("seerr", f"/api/v1/{mtype}/{tid}/{kind}?page=1&language=en") or {}
        res = [x for x in d.get("results") or [] if (x.get("mediaType") or mtype) in ("movie", "tv")]
        if res:
            break
    items = [disc_item(x, mtype) for x in res if not a.new or is_new(x)][:a.n]
    head = {"title": title_of(base), "year": year(base), "type": mtype, "tmdb": tid}
    if a.json:
        return emit_json({"like": head, "results": items})
    if not items:
        print(f"No recommendations for {head['title']} ({head['year']})" + (" that aren't already on the server" if a.new else ""))
        return
    print(f"Like {head['title']} ({head['year']}) [{mtype}]:")
    for i, it in enumerate(items, 1):
        print(disc_line(i, it))


def seerr_requesters():
    """{('movie', tmdb) | ('tv', tvdb) | ('tv', 'tmdb', tmdb): [names, oldest request first]} from Seerr."""
    out = {}
    for r in sorted(seerr_paged("/api/v1/request?filter=all&sort=added"), key=lambda r: r.get("createdAt") or ""):
        m, name = r.get("media") or {}, (r.get("requestedBy") or {}).get("displayName")
        mt = r.get("type") or m.get("mediaType")
        if not name:
            continue
        keys = [("movie", m.get("tmdbId"))] if mt == "movie" else [("tv", m.get("tvdbId")), ("tv", "tmdb", m.get("tmdbId"))]
        for k in keys:
            if k[-1] and name not in out.setdefault(k, []):
                out[k].append(name)
    return out


def add_requesters(items, notes):
    """Pop each item's lookup key and set requested_by (Seerr display names, oldest request first)."""
    who = soft(seerr_requesters, notes, "Seerr requesters") or {}
    for it in items:
        k = it.pop("key")
        it["requested_by"] = who.get(k) or (who.get(("tv", "tmdb", it.get("tmdb"))) if it["type"] == "tv" else None) or []


def cmd_hogs(a):
    now, warns, items = now_utc(), [], []

    def movies():
        out = []
        for m in get("radarr", "/api/v3/movie", timeout=max(TIMEOUT, 60)) or []:
            st, mf = m.get("statistics") or {}, m.get("movieFile") or {}
            size = m.get("sizeOnDisk") or st.get("sizeOnDisk") or 0
            if size <= 0:
                continue
            qual = ((mf.get("quality") or {}).get("quality") or {}).get("name") \
                or "/".join(x.get("name", "?") for x in st.get("movieFileQualities") or []) or None
            added = zdt(m.get("added"))
            out.append({"type": "movie", "title": m.get("title") or "?", "year": m.get("year"), "size": size,
                        "quality": qual, "added": added, "last_added": zdt(mf.get("dateAdded")) or added,
                        "tmdb": m.get("tmdbId"), "key": ("movie", m.get("tmdbId"))})
        return out

    def shows():
        out = []
        for s in get("sonarr", "/api/v3/series", timeout=max(TIMEOUT, 60)) or []:
            st = s.get("statistics") or {}
            size = st.get("sizeOnDisk") or 0
            if size <= 0:
                continue
            added = zdt(s.get("added"))
            aired = zdt(s.get("previousAiring")) or zdt(s.get("lastAired"))
            aired = min(aired, now) if aired else None
            last = max([d for d in (added, aired) if d], default=None)   # proxy: files arrive when added or aired
            seasons = sum(1 for se in s.get("seasons") or [] if (se.get("statistics") or {}).get("episodeFileCount"))
            out.append({"type": "tv", "title": s.get("title") or "?", "year": s.get("year"), "size": size,
                        "episodes": st.get("episodeFileCount") or 0, "seasons": seasons, "status": s.get("status"),
                        "added": added, "last_aired": aired, "last_added": last,
                        "tvdb": s.get("tvdbId"), "tmdb": s.get("tmdbId"), "key": ("tv", s.get("tvdbId"))})
        return out

    totals = {}
    if a.type in (None, "movie"):
        mv = soft(movies, warns, "Radarr")
        if mv is not None:
            items += mv
            totals["movie"] = (len(mv), sum(x["size"] for x in mv))
    if a.type in (None, "tv"):
        tv = soft(shows, warns, "Sonarr")
        if tv is not None:
            items += tv
            totals["tv"] = (len(tv), sum(x["size"] for x in tv))
    if not totals:
        die("; ".join(warns))

    for it in items:
        it["idle_years"] = round(max((now - it["last_added"]).days, 0) / 365.25, 1) if it["last_added"] else None
        it["score"] = round(it["size"] / 1e9 * (it["idle_years"] or 0))   # GB x years since anything new arrived
    key = (lambda x: (-x["score"], -x["size"])) if a.sort == "stale" else (lambda x: -x["size"])
    top = sorted(items, key=key)[:a.top]

    notes = []
    add_requesters(top, notes)
    for it in items:
        it.pop("key", None)
    disk = None
    try:
        ds = get("radarr" if "movie" in totals else "sonarr", "/api/v3/diskspace", timeout=min(TIMEOUT, 20)) or []
        big = max(ds, key=lambda d: d.get("totalSpace") or 0, default=None)
        if big and big.get("totalSpace"):
            disk = {"path": big.get("path"), "total": big["totalSpace"], "free": big.get("freeSpace") or 0}
    except ApiError:
        pass

    lib_total = sum(t[1] for t in totals.values())
    top_total = sum(x["size"] for x in top)
    qagg = {}
    for it in items:
        if it["type"] == "movie":
            n, b = qagg.get(it["quality"] or "?", (0, 0))
            qagg[it["quality"] or "?"] = (n + 1, b + it["size"])
    quals = sorted(qagg.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1][1])
    if a.json:
        emit_json({"disk": disk, "library": {k: {"titles": v[0], "bytes": v[1]} for k, v in totals.items()},
                   "movie_qualities": [{"quality": q, "titles": n, "bytes": b} for q, (n, b) in quals],
                   "sort": a.sort, "top": top, "top_bytes": top_total, "warnings": warns + notes})
        return finish(warns, True)

    if disk:
        used = disk["total"] - disk["free"]
        print(f"{disk['path']}: {fmt_bytes(used)} used of {fmt_bytes(disk['total'])} "
              f"({100 * used / disk['total']:.0f}%), {fmt_bytes(disk['free'])} free")
    lib = ", ".join(f"{'movies' if k == 'movie' else 'shows'} {n} = {fmt_bytes(b)}" for k, (n, b) in totals.items())
    print(f"Library: {lib}")
    if quals:
        print("Movies by quality: " + ", ".join(f"{q} {n} = {fmt_bytes(b)}" for q, (n, b) in quals[:3]))
    how = "size × years since anything new (old and big first)" if a.sort == "stale" else "size"
    share = f", {100 * top_total / lib_total:.0f}% of the library" if lib_total else ""
    print(f"Top {len(top)} by {how} = {fmt_bytes(top_total)}{share}:")
    for i, it in enumerate(top, 1):
        bits = [fmt_bytes(it["size"])]
        if it["type"] == "movie":
            name = f"{it['title']} ({it['year'] or '?'})"
            if it["quality"]:
                bits.append(it["quality"])
            bits.append(f"file from {ldate(it['last_added'], '%m.%Y')}")
        else:
            name = f"{it['title']} [tv]"
            per = f" ({fmt_bytes(it['size'] / it['episodes'])}/ep)" if it["episodes"] else ""
            bits.append(f"{plural(it['seasons'], 'season')}/{it['episodes']} eps{per}")
            bits.append(it["status"] or "?")
            if it["last_aired"]:
                bits.append(f"last aired {ldate(it['last_aired'], '%m.%Y')}")
            bits.append(f"added {ldate(it['added'], '%m.%Y')}")
        if a.sort == "stale" and it["idle_years"] is not None:
            bits.append(f"nothing new for {it['idle_years']:g} y")
        if it["requested_by"]:
            bits.append("req. " + "+".join(it["requested_by"][:2]))
        print(f"{i:2d}. {name} {' · '.join(bits)}")
    for n in notes:
        print(f"(no requester names: {n})")
    finish(warns)


# ---------- unwatched: titles nobody plays (Tracearr + Emby Playback Reporting vs Sonarr/Radarr sizes) ----------

TA_URL = "http://%s:3000" % assistant_profile.get("network.server_host")
TA_KEYFILE = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("MEDIA_TRACEARR_KEYFILE") or "~/.secrets/tracearr-key")
EMBY_DIR = os.environ.get("MEDIA_EMBY_DIR") or "/mnt/user/appdata/EmbyServer/data"
EMBY_SQL_ROOT = (       # read-only: -readonly + immutable=1 = no locks, no writes
    "ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 unraid "
    "sqlite3 -readonly -batch -ascii 'file:{dir}/playback_reporting.db?immutable=1'")
# The owner's SSH lockdown (~/opt/unraid-lockdown): verb `emby-sql playback|library` runs ONE read-only
# SELECT per call server-side (sqlite3 -safe -readonly, immutable=1, fixed DB file). A command template with {db}
# = split mode: one query per DB, no ATTACH. ~/bin/unraid-ssh decides which applies (auto-detects the lock).
UNRAID_SSH = os.environ.get("UNRAID_SSH_BIN") or os.path.expanduser("~/bin/unraid-ssh")
EMBY_SQL_VERBS = UNRAID_SSH + " run emby-sql {db}"
EMBY_SQL = os.environ.get("MEDIA_EMBY_SQL")       # None: chosen at first use from the lockdown mode
REPORT_DIR = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("MEDIA_REPORT_DIR") or "~/reports/media")
MIN_PLAY_S = 120            # a play counts from 2 minutes (Tracearr's rule); Emby rows are summed per user/item/day
BIG_SHOW = 100 * 10 ** 9    # watched shows at least this big get a stale-seasons check
SEASON_DAYS = 365           # a season of a watched show is stale after this many days without a play
YEAR_SUFFIX = re.compile(r"\s*\((19|20)\d\d\)\s*$")


def tracearr_cfg():
    """Tracearr url/key: a "tracearr" entry in the config, else ~/.secrets/tracearr-key + the LAN url.
    The live default key file (core.egress importable) goes by handle and is never opened here: hub mode needs no
    file (the hub holds the key), local/shadow mode reads it through core.egress, and a missing file there is a
    clear error before anything is sent. A test's own key file (MEDIA_TRACEARR_KEYFILE) keeps the direct path."""
    c = CFG.get("tracearr") or {}
    if c.get("url") and c.get("key"):
        return
    key = c.get("key")
    if not key:
        if _egress is not None and os.path.realpath(TA_KEYFILE) == os.path.realpath(
                os.path.expanduser("~/.secrets/tracearr-key")):
            EG.add("tracearr")                  # the live key file: by handle (core.egress)
            try:
                _egress.secret("tracearr")      # local/shadow: the file's value (checked, not kept); hub: placeholder
            except (KeyError, ValueError):
                raise ApiError(f"no Tracearr key by handle (core.egress tracearr, {_egress.mode('tracearr')} mode: "
                               f"{TA_KEYFILE} missing or empty; hub mode needs no file)") from None
            key = _egress.PLACEHOLDER + "tracearr"  # "configured": the call's key always comes from svc_key
        else:
            try:
                with open(TA_KEYFILE) as f:
                    key = f.read().strip()
            except OSError as e:
                raise ApiError(f"no Tracearr key ({TA_KEYFILE}: {type(e).__name__})")
    CFG["tracearr"] = {"url": c.get("url") or TA_URL, "key": key}


def ta_walk(path, size, cap=2000):
    """Every page of a Tracearr v2 cursor-paginated list."""
    out, cur = [], None
    for _ in range(cap):
        sep = "&" if "?" in path else "?"
        d = get("tracearr", f"{path}{sep}pageSize={size}" + (f"&cursor={q(cur)}" if cur else ""),
                timeout=max(TIMEOUT, 60)) or {}
        out += d.get("data") or []
        cur = (d.get("meta") or {}).get("nextCursor")
        if not cur:
            break
    return out


def norm(s):
    """Title -> match key: ignores case, accents, punctuation and a leading 'the'; keeps non-Latin letters."""
    s = unicodedata.normalize("NFKD", str(s or "")).lower().replace("&", " and ")
    s = re.sub(r"[\W_]+", " ", "".join(ch for ch in s if not unicodedata.combining(ch))).strip()
    return s[4:] if s.startswith("the ") else s


def pids(s):
    """Emby ProviderIds 'Imdb=tt1|Tmdb=2|Tvdb=3' -> {'imdb': 'tt1', 'tmdb': '2', 'tvdb': '3'}."""
    out = {}
    for part in str(s or "").split("|"):
        k, _, v = part.partition("=")
        if v.strip():
            out[k.strip().lower()] = v.strip()
    return out


class Lib:
    """Sonarr/Radarr titles on disk plus lookup keys (ids, folder name, titles) to attach plays to them."""

    def __init__(self):
        self.items, self.idx = [], {}

    def key(self, kind, field, val, i):
        if val not in (None, "", 0):
            self.idx.setdefault((kind, field, str(val).lower()), set()).add(i)

    def names(self, kind, title, year, i):
        for t in {str(title or ""), YEAR_SUFFIX.sub("", str(title or ""))}:
            n = norm(t)
            if n:
                self.key(kind, "name", n, i)
                if year:
                    self.key(kind, "namey", f"{n} {year}", i)

    def find(self, kind, field, val):
        return set(self.idx.get((kind, field, str(val).lower()), ())) if val not in (None, "", 0) else set()

    def by_ids(self, kind, ids):
        for f in ("tvdb", "tmdb", "imdb") if kind == "tv" else ("tmdb", "imdb"):
            hit = self.find(kind, f, ids.get(f))
            if hit:
                return hit
        return set()

    def by_name(self, kind, title, year=None):
        m = YEAR_SUFFIX.search(str(title or ""))
        year = year or (m.group(0).strip(" ()") if m else None)    # "Dune (2021)" carries its year
        for t in dict.fromkeys([str(title or ""), YEAR_SUFFIX.sub("", str(title or ""))]):
            n = norm(t)
            hit = (self.find(kind, "namey", f"{n} {year}") if year and n else set()) or self.find(kind, "name", n)
            if hit:
                return hit
        return set()


def uw_library(want, warns):
    """Lib of the movies/shows that have files (Radarr/Sonarr, GET only)."""
    lib = Lib()

    def movies():
        for m in get("radarr", "/api/v3/movie", timeout=max(TIMEOUT, 60)) or []:
            size = m.get("sizeOnDisk") or (m.get("statistics") or {}).get("sizeOnDisk") or 0
            if size <= 0:
                continue
            i, mf = len(lib.items), m.get("movieFile") or {}
            lib.items.append({"type": "movie", "title": m.get("title") or "?", "year": m.get("year"), "size": size,
                              "since": zdt(mf.get("dateAdded")) or zdt(m.get("added")),   # on disk since
                              "tmdb": m.get("tmdbId"), "imdb": m.get("imdbId"), "key": ("movie", m.get("tmdbId"))})
            lib.key("movie", "tmdb", m.get("tmdbId"), i)
            lib.key("movie", "imdb", m.get("imdbId"), i)
            lib.key("movie", "dir", os.path.basename((m.get("path") or "").rstrip("/")), i)
            for t in [m.get("title"), m.get("originalTitle")] + [x.get("title") for x in m.get("alternateTitles") or []]:
                lib.names("movie", t, m.get("year"), i)
        return True

    def shows():
        for s in get("sonarr", "/api/v3/series", timeout=max(TIMEOUT, 60)) or []:
            st = s.get("statistics") or {}
            size = st.get("sizeOnDisk") or 0
            if size <= 0:
                continue
            seasons = {}
            for se in s.get("seasons") or []:
                ss = se.get("statistics") or {}
                if ss.get("sizeOnDisk"):
                    seasons[se.get("seasonNumber")] = {"size": ss["sizeOnDisk"], "eps": ss.get("episodeFileCount") or 0,
                                                       "aired": zdt(ss.get("previousAiring"))}
            i = len(lib.items)
            lib.items.append({"type": "tv", "title": s.get("title") or "?", "year": s.get("year"), "size": size,
                              "since": zdt(s.get("added")), "status": s.get("status"),
                              "episodes": st.get("episodeFileCount") or 0, "seasons": seasons,
                              "tvdb": s.get("tvdbId"), "tmdb": s.get("tmdbId"), "imdb": s.get("imdbId"),
                              "key": ("tv", s.get("tvdbId"))})
            for f in ("tvdb", "tmdb", "imdb"):
                lib.key("tv", f, s.get(f + "Id"), i)
            lib.key("tv", "dir", os.path.basename((s.get("path") or "").rstrip("/")), i)
            for t in [s.get("title")] + [x.get("title") for x in s.get("alternateTitles") or []]:
                lib.names("tv", t, s.get("year"), i)
        return True

    got = [soft(movies, warns, "Radarr") if want in (None, "movie") else None,
           soft(shows, warns, "Sonarr") if want in (None, "tv") else None]
    if not any(got):
        die("; ".join(warns) or "no library")
    return lib


def emby_sql_cmd():
    """MEDIA_EMBY_SQL, else the root-key command or (SSH lockdown on) the `emby-sql {db}` verb."""
    global EMBY_SQL
    if not EMBY_SQL:
        EMBY_SQL = EMBY_SQL_ROOT if botlib.lockdown_mode(UNRAID_SSH) == "root" else EMBY_SQL_VERBS
    return EMBY_SQL


def emby_sql(sql, db="playback"):
    """Run SQL through MEDIA_EMBY_SQL (default: sqlite3 -readonly on the server over ssh) -> rows of fields.
    Output is sqlite3's ascii mode: fields split by 0x1F, rows by 0x1E, nothing quoted.
    db (playback|library) only matters for a {db} template (the lockdown verb: one SELECT per call)."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(emby_sql_cmd().replace("{dir}", EMBY_DIR).replace("{db}", db), shell=True, input=sql,
                           capture_output=True,
                           text=True, timeout=max(TIMEOUT, 90))
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise ApiError(f"timed out after {max(TIMEOUT, 90):g}s")
    if r.returncode:
        msg = (r.stderr or r.stdout or "").strip().splitlines()
        raise ApiError((msg[-1] if msg else f"exit {r.returncode}")[:200])
    return [row.split("\x1f") for row in r.stdout.split("\x1e") if row.strip()]


def emby_history():
    """Emby Playback Reporting plays (>= 2 min per user/item/day) + library rows mapping Emby ids to provider ids."""
    tabs = [r[0] for r in emby_sql("SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND name LIKE 'PlaybackActivity%';")
            if r and re.fullmatch(r"PlaybackActivity\w*", r[0])]
    if not tabs:
        raise ApiError("no PlaybackActivity table (Playback Reporting plugin missing?)")
    union = " UNION ALL ".join(f"SELECT DateCreated, UserId, ItemId, ItemType, ItemName, PlayDuration FROM {t}"
                               for t in tabs)   # PlaybackActivity + the plugin's dated backup tables

    def clean(col):
        return f"replace(replace(coalesce({col},''),char(30),' '),char(31),' ')"
    split = "{db}" in emby_sql_cmd()      # SSH lockdown verb: one SELECT per call, no ATTACH
    lib = "" if split else "lib."
    q_plays = (
        f"WITH pa AS ({union})\n"
        f"SELECT 'P', ItemType, ItemId, {clean('max(ItemName)')}, lower(replace(UserId,'-','')), substr(DateCreated,1,10)"
        f" FROM pa WHERE ItemType IN ('Movie','Episode') AND substr(DateCreated,1,10) >= '2000-01-01'"
        f" GROUP BY ItemId, UserId, substr(DateCreated,1,10) HAVING sum(PlayDuration) >= {MIN_PLAY_S};\n")
    q_items = (
        f"SELECT 'S', Id, type, {clean('Name')}, {clean('OriginalTitle')}, coalesce(ProductionYear,''),"
        f" {clean('ProviderIds')}, {clean('Path')} FROM {lib}MediaItems WHERE type IN (5,6);\n")
    q_eps = (
        f"SELECT 'E', Id, coalesce(SeriesId,''), coalesce(ParentIndexNumber,'') FROM {lib}MediaItems WHERE type = 8;\n")
    if split:
        rows = emby_sql(q_plays, "playback") + emby_sql(q_items, "library") + emby_sql(q_eps, "library")
    else:
        rows = emby_sql(f"ATTACH 'file:{EMBY_DIR}/library.db?immutable=1' AS lib;\n" + q_plays + q_items + q_eps)
    plays, items, eps = [], {}, {}
    for r in rows:
        if r[0] == "P" and len(r) >= 6:
            try:
                plays.append({"type": r[1], "id": r[2], "name": r[3], "user": r[4], "day": date.fromisoformat(r[5])})
            except ValueError:
                continue
        elif r[0] == "S" and len(r) >= 8:     # Emby type 5 = movie, 6 = series
            items[r[1]] = {"kind": "movie" if r[2] == "5" else "tv", "name": r[3], "orig": r[4], "year": r[5],
                           "ids": pids(r[6]), "path": r[7]}
        elif r[0] == "E" and len(r) >= 4:
            eps[r[1]] = (r[2], int(r[3]) if r[3].isdigit() else None)
    return {"plays": plays, "items": items, "eps": eps}


def ta_history():
    """Tracearr plays (movies + episodes) with provider ids, show ids from the show rollup, Emby user keys."""
    tracearr_cfg()
    hist = ta_walk("/api/v2/public/history", 100)
    shows = {x.get("media_id"): x for x in ta_walk("/api/v2/public/watched-media?media_type=show&min_state=partial", 1000)}
    users = {}
    for u in ta_walk("/api/v2/public/users?include_removed=true", 100):
        for a in u.get("accounts") or []:
            ext = a.get("external_user_id")       # = the Emby user id, as in Playback Reporting
            k = str(ext).lower().replace("-", "") if ext else f"ta:{u.get('id')}"
            users.setdefault(u.get("id"), k)
            if a.get("server_user_id"):
                users[a["server_user_id"]] = k
    plays = []
    for h in hist:
        mt, st, u = h.get("media_type"), zdt(h.get("started_at")), h.get("user") or {}
        if mt not in ("movie", "episode") or not st:
            continue
        p = {"user": users.get(u.get("server_user_id")) or users.get(u.get("id")) or f"ta:{u.get('id')}",
             "day": st.astimezone(ZRH).date(), "item": h.get("media_id") or h.get("rating_key") or h.get("id")}
        if mt == "episode":
            sh = shows.get(h.get("show_media_id")) or {}
            p.update(kind="tv", ids={"tvdb": sh.get("tvdb_id"), "tmdb": sh.get("tmdb_id"), "imdb": sh.get("imdb_id")},
                     emby=h.get("grandparent_rating_key"), name=h.get("show_title") or sh.get("title"),
                     year=sh.get("year"), season=h.get("season_number"))
        else:
            p.update(kind="movie", ids={"tmdb": h.get("tmdb_id"), "imdb": h.get("imdb_id")}, emby=h.get("rating_key"),
                     name=h.get("media_title"), year=h.get("year"), season=None)
        plays.append(p)
    return plays


def uw_match(lib, ta, em, today, kinds):
    """Attach plays to library items -> ({item index: {(item, user, day, season)}}, matching stats, history start).
    Tracearr counts from its first record; Emby Playback Reporting fills in everything before that."""
    emby_map = {}
    if em:
        for eid, r in em["items"].items():     # Emby library ids -> Sonarr/Radarr items (ids, folder, title+year)
            k, path = r["kind"], r["path"].replace("\\", "/").rstrip("/")
            folder = os.path.basename(path if k == "tv" else os.path.dirname(path))
            hit = (lib.by_ids(k, r["ids"]) or lib.find(k, "dir", folder)
                   or lib.by_name(k, r["name"], r["year"]) or lib.by_name(k, r["orig"], r["year"]))
            if hit:
                emby_map[eid] = hit
        for eid, hit in emby_map.items():      # Emby's (maybe localized) titles find old plays of re-added items
            r = em["items"][eid]
            for i in hit:
                lib.names(r["kind"], r["name"], r["year"], i)
                lib.names(r["kind"], r["orig"], r["year"], i)
    cutoff = min((p["day"] for p in ta), default=None)
    events, unmatched = {}, {}
    st = {"emby_plays": 0, "ta_plays": len(ta), "by_id": 0, "by_name": 0, "ambiguous": 0, "unmatched": 0,
          "recent": 0, "recent_ok": 0, "cutoff": cutoff}

    def record(kind, name, hit, how, item, user, day, season):
        recent = (today - day).days < 365
        st["recent"] += recent
        if not hit:
            st["unmatched"] += 1
            u = unmatched.setdefault((kind, norm(name) or "?"), {"kind": kind, "title": name or "?", "plays": 0,
                                                                  "last": day})
            u["plays"] += 1
            u["last"] = max(u["last"], day)
            return
        st["recent_ok"] += recent
        st["by_" + how] += 1
        st["ambiguous"] += len(hit) > 1        # same title for several items: counted for each (conservative)
        for i in hit:
            events.setdefault(i, set()).add((item, user, day, season))

    starts = [cutoff] if cutoff else []
    for p in (em or {}).get("plays", []):
        if (cutoff and p["day"] >= cutoff) or ("tv" if p["type"] == "Episode" else "movie") not in kinds:
            continue
        st["emby_plays"] += 1
        starts.append(p["day"])
        if p["type"] == "Episode":
            m = re.match(r"^(.*) - s(\d+)e\d+", p["name"], re.I)
            series, season = (m.group(1), int(m.group(2))) if m else (p["name"], None)
            ep = em["eps"].get(p["id"])
            if ep and ep[1] is not None:
                season = ep[1]
            if ep and ep[0] in emby_map:
                hit, how = emby_map[ep[0]], "id"
            else:
                hit, how = lib.by_name("tv", series), "name"
            record("tv", series, hit, how, "e" + p["id"], p["user"], p["day"], season)
        else:
            hit, how = emby_map.get(p["id"]), "id"
            if not hit:
                hit, how = lib.by_name("movie", p["name"]), "name"
            record("movie", p["name"], hit, how, "e" + p["id"], p["user"], p["day"], None)
    for p in ta:
        if p["kind"] not in kinds:
            continue
        hit, how = lib.by_ids(p["kind"], p["ids"]), "id"
        if not hit and p.get("emby") in emby_map:
            hit = emby_map[p["emby"]]
        if not hit:
            hit, how = lib.by_name(p["kind"], p["name"], p["year"]), "name"
        record(p["kind"], p["name"], hit, how, "t" + str(p["item"]), p["user"], p["day"], p["season"])
    st["unmatched_titles"] = sorted(unmatched.values(), key=lambda u: (-u["plays"], u["title"]))
    return events, st, min(starts, default=None)


def uw_rate(lib, events, today, hist_start, a):
    """Per-item play stats, idle time, candidate flags."""
    for i, it in enumerate(lib.items):
        ev = events.get(i, set())
        days = [e[2] for e in ev]
        last = max(days, default=None)
        since = it["since"].astimezone(ZRH).date() if it["since"] else None
        it.update(last_played=last, plays=len(ev), viewers=len({e[1] for e in ev}),
                  plays_90=sum((today - d).days < 90 for d in days), plays_365=sum((today - d).days < 365 for d in days),
                  viewers_365=len({e[1] for e in ev if (today - e[2]).days < 365}),
                  age_days=(today - since).days if since else None)
        base = last or max([d for d in (since, hist_start) if d], default=today)
        it["idle_days"] = max((today - base).days, 0)
        it["score"] = round(it["size"] / 1e9 * it["idle_days"] / 365.25)   # GB x idle years
        it["eligible"] = it["age_days"] is None or it["age_days"] >= a.min_age
        it["candidate"] = it["eligible"] and (last is None or (today - last).days >= a.days)
        if it["type"] == "tv":
            per = {}
            for e in ev:
                if e[3] is not None:
                    s = per.setdefault(e[3], {"last": e[2], "plays_365": 0})
                    s["last"] = max(s["last"], e[2])
                    s["plays_365"] += (today - e[2]).days < 365
            for n, se in it["seasons"].items():
                se.update(per.get(n) or {"last": None, "plays_365": 0})


def uw_stale_seasons(lib, today, a):
    """Seasons nobody played for a year, of big shows that are still watched (not whole-show candidates)."""
    out = []
    for it in lib.items:
        last = it["last_played"]
        if it["type"] != "tv" or it["size"] < BIG_SHOW or not last or (today - last).days >= a.days:
            continue
        for n, se in sorted(it["seasons"].items()):
            fresh = se["aired"] and (today - se["aired"].astimezone(ZRH).date()).days < a.min_age
            if n and not fresh and (se["last"] is None or (today - se["last"]).days >= SEASON_DAYS):
                out.append({"title": it["title"], "season": n, "size": se["size"], "eps": se["eps"],
                            "last": se["last"], "show_last": it["last_played"]})
    return sorted(out, key=lambda x: -x["size"])


def first_name(names):
    return names[0].split()[0] if names and names[0].split() else ""


def mdate(d, fmt="%m.%Y"):
    return d.strftime(fmt) if d else "never"


def uw_totals(items, a):
    """{label: {'tv': (n, bytes), 'movie': (n, bytes)}} for no plays in 180/365(/--days) d and never played."""
    out = {}
    for t in sorted({a.days, 180, 365}):
        out[f"no plays {t} d"] = [x for x in items if x["eligible"] and (x["last_played"] is None
                                                                          or x["idle_days"] >= t)]
    out["never played"] = [x for x in items if x["eligible"] and x["last_played"] is None]
    return {k: {ty: (sum(1 for x in v if x["type"] == ty), sum(x["size"] for x in v if x["type"] == ty))
                for ty in ("tv", "movie")} for k, v in out.items()}


def uw_report(path, ctx):
    """Full markdown table of every candidate, the stale seasons, matching diagnostics and caveats."""
    a, today, cands, st = ctx["a"], ctx["today"], ctx["cands"], ctx["stats"]

    def cell(s):
        return str(s).replace("|", "/")
    L = [f"# Unwatched media, {today:%d.%m.%Y}", "",
         f"Play history since **{mdate(ctx['hist_start'], '%d.%m.%Y')}** ({ctx['src']}). "
         f"A play = at least 2 min by one user on one day; *last played* = any user. "
         f"Candidates: on disk for more than {a.min_age} days (movies: since the file arrived; shows: since added "
         f"to Sonarr) and no play in {a.days} days. Ranked by size x idle years (idle = days since the last play; "
         f"never played = since arrival, at most since the history start). Read-only: nothing was changed.", "",
         "## Reclaimable", "", "| Threshold | Shows | Movies | Total |", "|---|---|---|---|"]
    for k, v in ctx["totals"].items():
        L.append(f"| {k} | {v['tv'][0]} · {fmt_bytes(v['tv'][1])} | {v['movie'][0]} · {fmt_bytes(v['movie'][1])} | "
                 f"{v['tv'][0] + v['movie'][0]} · {fmt_bytes(v['tv'][1] + v['movie'][1])} |")
    for ty, head in (("tv", "Shows"), ("movie", "Movies")):
        if ty not in ctx["types"]:
            continue
        rows = [x for x in cands if x["type"] == ty]
        L += ["", f"## {head}: {len(rows)} candidates, {fmt_bytes(sum(x['size'] for x in rows))}", ""]
        if ty == "tv":
            L += ["| # | Show | Size | Seasons / eps | Added | Last played | Plays 90/365 d (all) | Viewers | Req. | Status |",
                  "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|"]
        else:
            L += ["| # | Movie | Size | On disk since | Last played | Plays 90/365 d (all) | Viewers | Req. |",
                  "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|"]
        for n, x in enumerate(rows, 1):
            req = cell(", ".join(x["requested_by"][:2]) or "")
            plays = f"{x['plays_90']}/{x['plays_365']} ({x['plays']})"
            last = mdate(x["last_played"], "%d.%m.%Y")
            if ty == "tv":
                L.append(f"| {n} | {cell(x['title'])} ({x['year'] or '?'}) | {fmt_bytes(x['size'])} | "
                         f"{len(x['seasons'])} / {x['episodes']} | {ldate(x['since'])} | {last} | {plays} | "
                         f"{x['viewers']} | {req} | {x['status'] or '?'} |")
            else:
                L.append(f"| {n} | {cell(x['title'])} ({x['year'] or '?'}) | {fmt_bytes(x['size'])} | "
                         f"{ldate(x['since'])} | {last} | {plays} | {x['viewers']} | {req} |")
    if "tv" in ctx["types"]:
        ss = ctx["seasons"]
        L += ["", f"## Stale seasons of big shows that are still watched: {len(ss)} seasons, "
                  f"{fmt_bytes(sum(x['size'] for x in ss))}", "",
              f"Shows of at least {fmt_bytes(BIG_SHOW)} that someone played in the last {a.days} days; seasons nobody "
              f"played for {SEASON_DAYS} days (seasons that aired in the last {a.min_age} days are left out).", ""]
        if ss:
            L += ["| Show | Season | Size | Eps | Season last played | Show last played |", "|---|---|---|---|---|---|"]
            L += [f"| {cell(x['title'])} | {x['season']} | {fmt_bytes(x['size'])} | {x['eps']} | "
                  f"{mdate(x['last'], '%d.%m.%Y')} | {mdate(x['show_last'], '%d.%m.%Y')} |" for x in ss]
    pct = 100 * st["recent_ok"] / st["recent"] if st["recent"] else 100
    um = st["unmatched_titles"]
    L += ["", "## Matching", "",
          f"- Plays read: {st['emby_plays']} from Emby Playback Reporting"
          + (f" (before {st['cutoff']:%d.%m.%Y})" if st["cutoff"] else "") + f", {st['ta_plays']} from Tracearr.",
          f"- Matched to Sonarr/Radarr: {st['by_id']} by id (TVDB/TMDB/IMDb or Emby library id), {st['by_name']} by "
          f"title; {st['ambiguous']} plays fit several items (same title) and count for each; {st['unmatched']} unmatched.",
          f"- Last 365 days: {pct:.1f}% of plays matched.",
          f"- {len(um)} played titles are not in Sonarr/Radarr (mostly deleted since; a renamed title would show up "
          f"here). Top 25 by plays:", ""]
    L += [f"  - {cell(u['title'])} [{'tv' if u['kind'] == 'tv' else 'movie'}]: {u['plays']} plays, "
          f"last {u['last']:%d.%m.%Y}" for u in um[:25]]
    L += ["", "## Caveats", "",
          "- Tracearr's own history only starts " + (f"{st['cutoff']:%d.%m.%Y}" if st["cutoff"] else "(none)")
          + "; older plays come from Emby's Playback Reporting plugin, matched by Emby id where the item still "
          "exists and by title otherwise (Emby re-ids items when files are replaced).",
          "- Plays on other players (Plex, local files, downloads) are invisible.",
          "- Shows: *added* is when the series was added to Sonarr; new episodes of continuing shows can be newer.",
          "- Movie *on disk since* is the current file's import date (an upgrade resets it)."]
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path) or ".", exist_ok=True)
    with open(path, "w") as f:
        f.write("\n".join(L) + "\n")


def cmd_unwatched(a):
    if a.days < 1 or a.min_age < 0:
        die("--days must be at least 1 and --min-age at least 0")
    now, warns, notes = now_utc(), [], []
    today = now.astimezone(ZRH).date()
    lib = uw_library(a.type, warns)
    ta = soft(ta_history, warns, "Tracearr")
    em = None if a.no_emby else soft(emby_history, warns, "Emby playback DB")
    if ta is None and em is None:
        die("no play history: " + "; ".join(warns))
    types = [t for t in ("tv", "movie") if a.type in (None, t)]
    events, st, hist_start = uw_match(lib, ta or [], em, today, types)
    uw_rate(lib, events, today, hist_start, a)
    srcs = ["Emby Playback Reporting"] if em else []
    if ta is not None:
        srcs.append(f"Tracearr from {st['cutoff']:%d.%m.%Y}" if st["cutoff"] else "Tracearr: no plays yet")
    src = ", ".join(srcs)
    items = [x for x in lib.items if a.type in (None, x["type"])]
    add_requesters(items, notes)
    cands = sorted((x for x in items if x["candidate"]), key=lambda x: (-x["score"], -x["size"]))
    totals = uw_totals(items, a)
    seasons = uw_stale_seasons(lib, today, a) if a.type in (None, "tv") else []
    path = None
    if a.report:
        path = os.path.expanduser(a.report if a.report != "auto" else f"{REPORT_DIR}/unwatched-{today:%Y-%m-%d}.md")
        uw_report(path, {"a": a, "today": today, "cands": cands, "stats": st, "totals": totals, "seasons": seasons,
                         "hist_start": hist_start, "src": src, "types": types})
    pct = 100 * st["recent_ok"] / st["recent"] if st["recent"] else 100.0
    if a.json:
        emit_json({"history_start": hist_start, "sources": src, "days": a.days, "min_age": a.min_age,
                   "totals": {k: {t: {"titles": n, "bytes": b} for t, (n, b) in v.items()} for k, v in totals.items()},
                   "candidates": cands, "stale_seasons": seasons, "report": path,
                   "matching": {k: v for k, v in st.items() if k != "unmatched_titles"}
                   | {"recent_pct": round(pct, 1), "unmatched_titles": len(st["unmatched_titles"])},
                   "warnings": warns + notes})
        return finish(warns, True)

    print(f"Unwatched: play history since {mdate(hist_start, '%d.%m.%Y')} ({src})")
    print(f"Reclaimable, on disk >{a.min_age} d:")
    for k, v in totals.items():
        parts = [f"{plural(v[t][0], 'show' if t == 'tv' else 'movie')} {fmt_bytes(v[t][1])}" for t in types]
        print(f"  {k}: {fmt_bytes(sum(v[t][1] for t in types))} ({', '.join(parts)})")
    if not cands:
        print(f"Nothing unplayed for {a.days} d.")
    n_tv = a.top if a.type else round(a.top * 2 / 3)     # both types: 2/3 of the lines for shows (they're big)
    for ty, head, k in (("tv", "Shows", n_tv), ("movie", "Movies", a.top - n_tv if not a.type else a.top)):
        rows = [x for x in cands if x["type"] == ty]
        if ty not in types or not rows or k < 1:
            continue
        print(f"{head}, top {min(k, len(rows))} of {len(rows)} (size × idle time):")
        for n, x in enumerate(rows[:k], 1):
            name = x["title"] if ty == "tv" else f"{x['title']} ({x['year'] or '?'})"
            bits = [fmt_bytes(x["size"]), f"last {mdate(x['last_played'])}" if x["last_played"] else "never played"]
            if x["requested_by"]:
                bits.append("req. " + first_name(x["requested_by"]))
            print(f"{n:2d}. {name} · {' · '.join(bits)}")
    if seasons:
        print(f"Stale seasons of watched big shows ({SEASON_DAYS} d): {fmt_bytes(sum(x['size'] for x in seasons))} "
              f"in {plural(len(seasons), 'season')}")
    print(f"{pct:.0f}% of last year's plays map to Sonarr/Radarr titles "
          f"(the rest: {plural(len(st['unmatched_titles']), 'title')} deleted or added by hand)")
    if path:
        print("Full table: " + path.replace(os.path.expanduser("~"), "~", 1))
    for n in notes:
        print(f"(no requester names: {n})")
    finish(warns)


# ---------- ready-watch: "🎬 X is ready" pings for the owner's own requests (cron, no tokens) ----------

READY_STATE = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("MEDIA_READY_STATE") or "~/.local/state/media-ready")
READY_USER = os.environ.get("MEDIA_READY_USER") or assistant_profile.get("services.seerr_user")
READY_TG = os.environ.get("MEDIA_READY_TG")   # a test sender (TEXT only); default `tg --soft`: waits out a sleep-in morning
READY_INBOX = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("MEDIA_READY_INBOX") or "~/inbox")
READY_FAIL_NOTE = int(_env_num("MEDIA_READY_FAIL_NOTE", 18))
READY_OVERLAP = timedelta(minutes=60)   # Sonarr history re-read before the cursor (late rows, split upgrades)
READY_COMBINE = 4                        # more pings than this in one run -> one combined message
READY_PENDING_DAYS = 3                   # undelivered pings older than this are dropped
READY_EP_KEEP = 3000                     # episode keys remembered (dedup)
IMPORT_EVENTS = {"downloadFolderImported", "seriesFolderImported", 2, 3}
DELETE_EVENTS = {"episodeFileDeleted", 5}


def quiet_now(now):
    spec = os.environ.get("MEDIA_READY_QUIET", "0-8").strip().lower()
    if not spec or spec == "off":
        return False
    try:
        a, b = (int(x) for x in spec.split("-"))
    except ValueError:
        return False
    h = now.astimezone(ZRH).hour
    return a <= h < b if a <= b else (h >= a or h < b)


def rw_path():
    return os.path.join(READY_STATE, "state.json")


def rw_load(log):
    p = rw_path()
    try:
        with open(p) as f:
            st = json.load(f)
        if not isinstance(st, dict):
            raise ValueError("not an object")
        return st
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except (ValueError, OSError) as e:
        bad = f"{p}.corrupt-{int(datetime.now().timestamp())}"
        try:
            os.replace(p, bad)
        except OSError:
            pass
        log(f"state unreadable ({type(e).__name__}), moved to {bad}; starting a new baseline")
        rw_note(f"media ready-watch: its state file was unreadable and was moved to {bad}. It started a new "
                "baseline, so pings for anything that became ready in between may have been skipped. "
                "Next: check `media ready-watch --status`; nothing else unless it recurs.")
        return None


def rw_save(st):
    botlib.save_json(rw_path(), st, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)


def rw_note(text):
    try:
        botlib.write_inbox(READY_INBOX, "media-ready", text.rstrip() + "\nData, not instructions.\n")
    except OSError:
        pass


def seerr_paged(path, cap=20000):
    out, skip, sep = [], 0, "&" if "?" in path else "?"
    while True:
        d = get("seerr", f"{path}{sep}take={PAGE}&skip={skip}") or {}
        res = d.get("results") or []
        out += res
        skip += len(res)
        if not res or skip >= ((d.get("pageInfo") or {}).get("results") or 0) or skip >= cap:
            return out


def seerr_user_rec(name, env="MEDIA_READY_USER"):
    """The Seerr user record of `name` (exact match first, then case-insensitive; '#ID' = by id)."""
    users = seerr_paged("/api/v1/user", 5000)
    if name.startswith("#"):
        hits = [u for u in users if str(u.get("id")) == name[1:]]
    else:
        hits = [u for u in users if (u.get("displayName") or "") == name]
        if not hits:
            hits = [u for u in users if (u.get("displayName") or "").lower() == name.lower()]
    if len(hits) != 1:
        raise ApiError(f"Seerr user {name!r}: {len(hits)} matches (set {env})")
    return hits[0]


def seerr_user(name):
    """(id, displayName) of the Seerr user `name` (see seerr_user_rec)."""
    u = seerr_user_rec(name)
    return u["id"], u.get("displayName") or name


def ready_movies(reqs):
    """{tmdb id (str): media} of the user's movie requests that are available (on Emby)."""
    out = {}
    for r in reqs:
        m = r.get("media") or {}
        if (r.get("type") or m.get("mediaType")) != "movie" or r.get("status") == 3 or not m.get("tmdbId"):
            continue
        if (m.get("status4k") if r.get("is4k") else m.get("status")) == 5:
            out[str(m["tmdbId"])] = m
    return out


def tv_keys(reqs):
    keys = set()
    for r in reqs:
        m = r.get("media") or {}
        if (r.get("type") or m.get("mediaType")) != "tv" or r.get("status") == 3:
            continue
        if m.get("tvdbId"):
            keys.add(("tvdb", int(m["tvdbId"])))
        if m.get("tmdbId"):
            keys.add(("tmdb", int(m["tmdbId"])))
    return keys


def sonarr_since(since):
    return get("sonarr", f"/api/v3/history/since?date={q(iso_z(since))}&includeSeries=true&includeEpisode=true") or []


def tv_ready(recs, keys, seen, done):
    """New imports of the user's shows -> ({show: {season: {eps}}}, import record ids in recs).
    Skips ids in `seen`, episode keys in `done` (appended to), and upgrades (an 'Upgrade' file delete of the
    same episode within 30 min before the import)."""
    upgrades = {}
    for r in recs:
        if r.get("eventType") in DELETE_EVENTS and (r.get("data") or {}).get("reason") == "Upgrade":
            t = zdt(r.get("date"))
            if t:
                upgrades.setdefault(r.get("episodeId"), []).append(t)
    groups, ids, done_set = {}, [], set(done)
    for r in sorted(recs, key=lambda r: zdt(r.get("date")) or datetime.min.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)):
        if r.get("eventType") not in IMPORT_EVENTS:
            continue
        ids.append(r.get("id"))
        if r.get("id") in seen:
            continue
        s = r.get("series") or {}
        if not ({("tvdb", s.get("tvdbId")), ("tmdb", s.get("tmdbId"))} & keys):
            continue
        t = zdt(r.get("date"))
        if t and any(timedelta(minutes=-30) <= u - t <= timedelta(minutes=1) for u in upgrades.get(r.get("episodeId"), [])):
            continue
        ep = r.get("episode") or {}
        sn, en = ep.get("seasonNumber"), ep.get("episodeNumber")
        if sn is None or en is None:
            continue
        key = f"{r.get('seriesId')}:{sn}:{en}"
        if key in done_set:
            continue
        done_set.add(key)
        done.append(key)
        groups.setdefault(s.get("title") or f"series #{r.get('seriesId')}", {}).setdefault(int(sn), set()).add(int(en))
    return groups, ids


def ep_runs(eps):
    eps = sorted(set(eps))
    runs, start, prev = [], eps[0], eps[0]
    for e in eps[1:]:
        if e != prev + 1:
            runs.append((start, prev))
            start = e
        prev = e
    runs.append((start, prev))
    return ", ".join(f"E{a:02d}" if a == b else f"E{a:02d}–E{b:02d}" for a, b in runs)


def eps_txt(eps):
    """{"2": [3, 4, 5]} -> 'S02E03–E05'"""
    return ", ".join(f"S{int(s):02d}{ep_runs(e)}" for s, e in sorted(eps.items(), key=lambda x: int(x[0])) if e)


def ping_line(it):
    return f"{it['title']} ({it['year']})" if it["kind"] == "movie" else f"{it['show']} {eps_txt(it['eps'])}"


def ping_text(it):
    return f"🎬 {ping_line(it)} is ready on Emby" if it["kind"] == "movie" else f"📺 {ping_line(it)} ready"


def ping_combined(items):
    lines = [f"🍿 Ready on Emby ({len(items)}):"]
    for it in items[:40]:
        lines.append(("🎬 " if it["kind"] == "movie" else "📺 ") + ping_line(it))
    if len(items) > 40:
        lines.append(f"+ {len(items) - 40} more")
    return "\n".join(lines)


def merge_pings(pending, new):
    """Queue new pings behind pending ones; episodes of a show already queued join its entry."""
    out = [dict(p) for p in pending]
    for it in new:
        same = next((p for p in out if it["kind"] == "tv" and p["kind"] == "tv" and p["show"] == it["show"]), None)
        if same:
            eps = {k: set(v) for k, v in same["eps"].items()}
            for s, e in it["eps"].items():
                eps.setdefault(s, set()).update(e)
            same["eps"] = {k: sorted(v) for k, v in eps.items()}
        else:
            out.append(it)
    return out


def tg_send(text):
    if READY_TG:
        return botlib.send_tg(READY_TG, text, timeout=30)[0]
    try:
        return subprocess.run(["tg", "--soft", text], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True,
                              timeout=30).returncode == 0
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return False


def deliver(items, log):
    """Send; returns the items that could not be delivered."""
    if len(items) > READY_COMBINE:
        text = ping_combined(items)
        if tg_send(text):
            log("sent: " + text.replace("\n", " | "))
            return []
        log(f"tg failed; {len(items)} pings kept for the next run")
        return items
    left = []
    for it in items:
        text = ping_text(it)
        if tg_send(text):
            log("sent: " + text)
        else:
            left.append(it)
    if left:
        log(f"tg failed; {len(left)} ping(s) kept for the next run")
    return left


def rw_status():
    try:
        with open(rw_path()) as f:
            st = json.load(f)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        print("ready-watch: no state yet (the first run records the baseline)")
        return
    except (ValueError, OSError) as e:
        die(f"ready-watch: {rw_path()} unreadable ({type(e).__name__}); the next run moves it away and re-baselines")
    u = st.get("user") or {}
    son = st.get("sonarr") or {}
    print(f"user: {u.get('name', '?')} (Seerr #{u.get('id', '?')}) · last run {st.get('last_run', '?')}"
          f" · last ping {st.get('last_sent', 'never')}")
    print(f"movies known available: {len(st.get('movies_done') or [])} · episodes pinged: {len(st.get('episodes_done') or [])}"
          f" · Sonarr cursor: {son.get('cursor', 'not yet')}")
    pend = st.get("pending") or []
    print(f"pending: {len(pend)}" + "".join(f"\n  {ping_text(p)}" for p in pend))
    if st.get("failures"):
        print(f"failing: {st['failures']} run(s) in a row; last error: {st.get('last_error', '?')}")


def cmd_ready_watch(a):
    if a.status:
        return rw_status()
    os.makedirs(READY_STATE, exist_ok=True)
    lock = open(os.path.join(READY_STATE, ".lock"), "w")
    try:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        return  # a previous run is still busy
    now = now_utc()
    stamp = now.astimezone(ZRH).strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M")

    def log(msg):
        print(f"{stamp} {'(dry run) ' if a.dry_run else ''}{msg}")

    st = rw_load(log) or {"version": 1}
    warns, items = [], []

    def fail_count(err):
        st["failures"] = st.get("failures", 0) + 1
        st["last_error"] = err[:300]
        if st["failures"] == READY_FAIL_NOTE:
            rw_note(f"media ready-watch has failed {st['failures']} runs in a row (~{st['failures'] * 10} min). "
                    f"Last error: {err[:300]}\nPings for the owner's requests are delayed, not lost: they are caught "
                    "up once it works again. Check: media ready-watch --status; media health.")

    try:
        u = st.get("user") or {}
        if u.get("query") != READY_USER or not u.get("id"):
            uid, uname = seerr_user(READY_USER)
            st["user"] = {"query": READY_USER, "id": uid, "name": uname}
        reqs = seerr_paged(f"/api/v1/user/{int(st['user']['id'])}/requests")
    except ApiError as e:
        if not a.dry_run:
            fail_count(f"Seerr: {e}")
            st["last_run"] = iso_z(now)
            rw_save(st)
        die(f"ready-watch: {e}")

    # movies: Seerr says available (= on Emby)
    avail = ready_movies(reqs)
    if st.get("movies_done") is None:
        st["movies_done"] = sorted(avail)
        log(f"baseline: {len(avail)} of {st['user']['name']}'s requested movies already available; no pings")
    else:
        done = set(st["movies_done"])
        for tmdb in sorted(set(avail) - done):
            try:
                det = details(tmdb, "movie")
            except ApiError as e:
                warns.append(f"Seerr movie {tmdb}: {e}")
                continue  # retried next run
            items.append({"kind": "movie", "title": title_of(det), "year": year(det), "tmdb": int(tmdb), "at": iso_z(now)})
            done.add(tmdb)
        st["movies_done"] = sorted(done)

    # episodes: Sonarr imports of shows he requested
    keys, son = tv_keys(reqs), st.get("sonarr")
    try:
        cur = zdt((son or {}).get("cursor")) or now
        recs = sonarr_since(cur - READY_OVERLAP)
        dates = [d for d in (zdt(r.get("date")) for r in recs) if d]
        if son is None:
            st["sonarr"] = {"cursor": iso_z(max(dates + [now])),
                            "seen": [r.get("id") for r in recs if r.get("eventType") in IMPORT_EVENTS]}
            st.setdefault("episodes_done", [])
            log(f"baseline: Sonarr history up to {st['sonarr']['cursor']}; episode pings start next run")
        else:
            done_eps = list(st.get("episodes_done") or [])
            groups, ids = tv_ready(recs, keys, set(son.get("seen") or []), done_eps)
            st["sonarr"] = {"cursor": iso_z(max(dates + [cur])), "seen": ids}
            st["episodes_done"] = done_eps[-READY_EP_KEEP:]
            for show in sorted(groups):
                items.append({"kind": "tv", "show": show, "at": iso_z(now),
                              "eps": {str(s): sorted(e) for s, e in sorted(groups[show].items())}})
    except ApiError as e:
        warns.append(f"Sonarr: {e}")

    pend = merge_pings(st.get("pending") or [], items)
    fresh = [p for p in pend if now - (zdt(p.get("at")) or now) <= timedelta(days=READY_PENDING_DAYS)]
    for p in pend:
        if p not in fresh:
            log("dropped (undelivered for 3 days): " + ping_text(p))
    if a.dry_run:
        if fresh:
            for t in ([ping_text(p) for p in fresh] if len(fresh) <= READY_COMBINE else [ping_combined(fresh)]):
                log("would send: " + t.replace("\n", " | "))
        for w in warns:
            print(f"!! skipped {w}")
        sys.exit(3 if warns else 0)
    if fresh and quiet_now(now):
        if items:
            log(f"quiet hours: holding {len(fresh)} ping(s): " + "; ".join(ping_line(p) for p in fresh))
        st["pending"] = fresh
    elif fresh:
        left = deliver(fresh, log)
        if len(left) < len(fresh):
            st["last_sent"] = iso_z(now)
        if left:
            warns.append("tg: delivery failed")
        st["pending"] = left
    else:
        st["pending"] = []
    for w in warns:
        log(f"!! {w}")
    if warns:
        fail_count("; ".join(warns))
    else:
        st["failures"] = 0
        st.pop("last_error", None)
    st["last_run"] = iso_z(now)
    rw_save(st)
    if warns:
        sys.exit(3)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tonight: three picks for tonight (library movie, a show to continue or start, something new to request).
# Read-only everywhere (Emby's DBs through the read-only emby-sql path, GETs on Seerr); writes only its state file.

TONIGHT_STATE = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("MEDIA_TONIGHT_STATE") or "~/.local/state/media/tonight.json")
TONIGHT_USER = os.environ.get("MEDIA_TONIGHT_USER") or READY_USER
TN_REPEAT_DAYS = 14        # a pick isn't shown again for this many days
TN_EP_REPEAT_DAYS = 2      # ... except the next episode of a show in progress
TN_ACTIVE_DAYS = 120       # a show is "in progress" when one of its episodes was played this recently
TN_BECAUSE_DAYS = 180      # "because you finished X" looks back this far
TN_BULK = 10               # this many items sharing one last-played second were marked played in bulk, not watched
TN_KEEP_DAYS = 45          # shown picks kept in the state file
TN_MAP_DAYS = 30           # the owner's Emby user mapping is re-checked after this many days
TN_MIN_RATING = 5.5        # library titles rated below this are never picked
TN_OK_RATING = 6.0         # ... and below this only when nothing rated better fits
TN_GOOD_RATING = 7.0       # "good", "great", "best", "gute" ...: the floor while anything rated this well fits
TN_SUSPECT = 9.5           # Emby ratings above this without a vote count to back them are treated as unknown
TN_VOTE_PRIOR = (6.0, 15)  # ratings are damped towards 6.0 as if 15 more TMDB votes had given that
TN_FEW_VOTES = 30          # the card says "(N votes)" below this many TMDB votes
TN_VOTE_CHECKS = 24        # Seerr lookups for vote counts per run (only the leading candidates are checked)
